{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba test/yang/typescript_callsite_test.cljc | sed -n '1,380p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t(ns yang.typescript-callsite-test\n     2\t  \"Contract C1 for production yang.typescript (Addendum A, design §2): the\n     3\t   `:yang/call-site 1` frontend-metadata annotation of every final\n     4\t   `:application` occurrence on this frontend's compilation and publication\n     5\t   paths, and the complete-coverage validation a consumer runs against\n     6\t   canonical rows. Mirrors `yang.clojure-callsite-test`'s shape: the\n     7\t   equality gate, the boundary, the validation failures,\n     8\t   safepoint-independence and canonical invariance.\n     9\t\n    10\t   THREE key families, never conflated:\n    11\t\n    12\t   - `:yang/call-site` (this file) is COMPILE-TIME application-occurrence\n    13\t     frontend metadata. It rides the EXISTING generic side table:\n    14\t     projection (`yin.vm/ast-side-tables`) drops it from canonical rows and\n    15\t     emits `[origin root-address path :yang/call-site 1]`. The walk is\n    16\t     `yang.core.uast/annotate-call-sites`; the ts frontend consumes it and\n    17\t     re-mints nothing.\n    18\t   - `:yang/site` is the SAFEPPOINT mark. It travels as NODE METADATA, not\n    19\t     as a plain node key; `safepoint-independence-test` pins the\n    20\t     distinction. The design forbids aliasing one to the other.\n    21\t   - `cell/dsg__new-provenance` / `cell/dsg__provenance` are the EXCEPTION\n    22\t     TRACK's runtime VM primitive doors (landed `8c10c5b7`), minting and\n    23\t     reading retained-condition provenance while a task runs. Different\n    24\t     family, different lifetime, different table: they are host primitives\n    25\t     a guest calls, never frontend metadata a lowering emits. The\n    26\t     TypeScript prelude does not reach them at all — it authenticates a\n    27\t     retained condition through its own sealed companion cell — and\n    28\t     `export-audit-pin-test` pins both halves of that: no `dsg__` door\n    29\t     appears in a `js` definition, and no C1 surface leaks into the\n    30\t     guest-visible `js`/`jssp` exports or runtime keys.\n    31\t\n    32\t   Portable (JVM/Node/Dart). Every fixture is a hand-built CST packet from\n    33\t   `yang.typescript.antlr.lower-portable-test`, so no local parser is\n    34\t   involved: the same source-derived packet lowers to the same occurrence\n    35\t   coordinates on every lane. That is the cross-host EQUALITY GATE the\n    36\t   orchestrator ruled (1795010000000) to be part of THIS frontend's own\n    37\t   acceptance — same source on the ts lanes, identical coordinates, and\n    38\t   never a cross-frontend comparison (different frontends compile\n    39\t   different sources, so there is no cross-frontend coordinate to equal).\n    40\t   `cross-host-equality-test` is the local half of that gate; the full lane\n    41\t   matrix is the orchestrator's, on shiva/jupiter.\"\n    42\t  (:require [clojure.string :as str]\n    43\t            [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n    44\t            [dao.jing.cbor :as cbor]\n    45\t            [yang.clojure :as yang]\n    46\t            [yang.core.uast :as u]\n    47\t            [yang.safepoint :as safepoint]\n    48\t            [yang.typescript.antlr.lower :as lower]\n    49\t            [yang.typescript.antlr.lower-portable-test :as portable]\n    50\t            [yang.typescript.antlr.prelude :as prelude]\n    51\t            [yang.typescript.antlr.safepoint :as hooks]\n    52\t            [yin.vm :as vm]\n    53\t            [yin.vm.encoder :as encoder]\n    54\t            [yin.vm.semantic.linearize :as sr-linearize]))\n    55\t\n    56\t\n    57\t;; =============================================================================\n    58\t;; Fixtures: hand-built CST packets, so every lane compiles the same input\n    59\t;; =============================================================================\n    60\t\n    61\t(def ^:private var-x\n    62\t  \"`var x = 1;`\"\n    63\t  (portable/program (portable/var-stmt \"var\" \"x\" (portable/num-expr \"1\"))))\n    64\t\n    65\t\n    66\t(def ^:private log-x\n    67\t  \"`var x = 7; console.log(x);` — a member call, so the generated\n    68\t   `js/get-value` / `js/call` dispatch is in the tree.\"\n    69\t  (portable/program\n    70\t    (portable/var-stmt \"var\" \"x\" (portable/num-expr \"7\"))\n    71\t    (portable/log-stmt (portable/name-expr \"x\"))))\n    72\t\n    73\t\n    74\t(def ^:private while-x\n    75\t  \"`while (x) ;` — one `:loop` safepoint site.\"\n    76\t  (portable/program\n    77\t    [:iterationStatement\n    78\t     [\"While\" \"while\"] [\"OpenParen\" \"(\"]\n    79\t     [:expressionSequence (portable/name-expr \"x\")]\n    80\t     [\"CloseParen\" \")\"]\n    81\t     [:statement [:emptyStatement_ [\"SemiColon\" \";\"]]]]))\n    82\t\n    83\t\n    84\t(def ^:private function-f\n    85\t  \"`function f() {}` — one `:call` safepoint site.\"\n    86\t  (portable/program\n    87\t    [:functionDeclaration\n    88\t     [\"Function_\" \"function\"]\n    89\t     [:identifier [\"Identifier\" \"f\"]]\n    90\t     [:callSignature [\"OpenParen\" \"(\"] [\"CloseParen\" \")\"]]\n    91\t     [\"OpenBrace\" \"{\"]\n    92\t     [:functionBody]\n    93\t     [\"CloseBrace\" \"}\"]]))\n    94\t\n    95\t\n    96\t;; =============================================================================\n    97\t;; The projection and the two coordinate derivations\n    98\t;; =============================================================================\n    99\t\n   100\t(def ^:private medium\n   101\t  \"This test's program medium: the origin's first opaque coordinate, which\n   102\t   the admitting composition supplies and the frontend never mints.\"\n   103\t  :yang.ts/callsite-test)\n   104\t\n   105\t\n   106\t(def ^:private token \"ts-callsite-1\")\n   107\t\n   108\t\n   109\t(def ^:private origin [:source medium token 0])\n   110\t\n   111\t\n   112\t(defn- project\n   113\t  \"The canonical rows and the generic frontend-metadata side table of `ast`\n   114\t   under this test's admission origin, through the production encoder.\"\n   115\t  [ast]\n   116\t  (let [projected (encoder/project (encoder/source-envelope medium token [ast]))]\n   117\t    {:tree (first (:yin/batch projected))\n   118\t     :metadata (:yin/frontend-metadata projected)}))\n   119\t\n   120\t\n   121\t(defn- eligible-under\n   122\t  \"The eligible C1 site set of canonical `tree` under `origin`, derived\n   123\t   here directly from the occurrence relation and the row tags —\n   124\t   independently of the producer's own walk.\"\n   125\t  [tree origin]\n   126\t  (into #{}\n   127\t        (map (fn [[root path]] [origin root path]))\n   128\t        (vm/application-occurrences tree)))\n   129\t\n   130\t\n   131\t(defn- eligible\n   132\t  [tree]\n   133\t  (eligible-under tree origin))\n   134\t\n   135\t\n   136\t(defn- occurrence-pairs\n   137\t  \"The `[root-address path]` of every `:application` occurrence of\n   138\t   canonical `tree`: the projection a consumer derives from canonical rows\n   139\t   alone, origin-free.\"\n   140\t  [tree]\n   141\t  (into #{} (map (fn [[root path]] [root path])) (vm/application-occurrences tree)))\n   142\t\n   143\t\n   144\t(defn- marked-under\n   145\t  \"The `[origin root-address path]` of the C1 rows of `metadata` claimed\n   146\t   under `origin` — the ORIGIN-SCOPED marker set. Filtering on the row's\n   147\t   own origin coordinate is what makes the query meaningful: a relation\n   148\t   admitted under a DIFFERENT origin answers empty here, which is how\n   149\t   `stage-envelope-test` proves the frontend stamps no origin of its own.\n   150\t   (The origin-free projection a consumer derives from canonical rows alone\n   151\t   is `marked-pairs`, below.)\"\n   152\t  [metadata origin]\n   153\t  (into #{}\n   154\t        (comp (filter #(and (= :yang/call-site (nth % 3))\n   155\t                            (= origin (nth % 0))))\n   156\t              (map (fn [[o r path _ _]] [o r path])))\n   157\t        metadata))\n   158\t\n   159\t\n   160\t(defn- marked\n   161\t  [metadata]\n   162\t  (marked-under metadata origin))\n   163\t\n   164\t\n   165\t(defn- marked-pairs\n   166\t  \"The `[root-address path]` projection of a C1 marker relation.\"\n   167\t  [metadata]\n   168\t  (into #{}\n   169\t        (comp (filter #(= :yang/call-site (nth % 3)))\n   170\t              (map (fn [[_ r path _ _]] [r path])))\n   171\t        metadata))\n   172\t\n   173\t\n   174\t(defn- marker-rows\n   175\t  [metadata]\n   176\t  (filterv #(= :yang/call-site (nth % 3)) metadata))\n   177\t\n   178\t\n   179\t(defn- failure-rule\n   180\t  [f]\n   181\t  (try (f) ::no-failure\n   182\t       (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Exception :cljs :default) e\n   183\t         (:rule (ex-data e)))))\n   184\t\n   185\t\n   186\t(defn- nodes\n   187\t  [tree]\n   188\t  (tree-seq #(or (map? %) (sequential? %))\n   189\t            #(if (map? %) (vals %) %)\n   190\t            tree))\n   191\t\n   192\t\n   193\t(defn- strip-call-sites\n   194\t  \"`node` with every C1 marker removed, at every depth the row grammar\n   195\t   knows. Node metadata and every other key survive, so the answer is\n   196\t   exactly the tree this frontend answered before the adoption.\"\n   197\t  [node]\n   198\t  (let [slots (get vm/semantic-bytecode-grammar (:type node))]\n   199\t    (reduce (fn [n [field kind]]\n   200\t              (case kind\n   201\t                :node (update n field strip-call-sites)\n   202\t                :nodes (update n field #(mapv strip-call-sites %))\n   203\t                n))\n   204\t            (dissoc node :yang/call-site)\n   205\t            slots)))\n   206\t\n   207\t\n   208\t(defn- marked-operator-names\n   209\t  \"The operator name of every C1-marked `:application` of `ast`: the K of\n   210\t   each generated dispatch. An application whose operator is a lambda (a\n   211\t   scope's cell binding, a sequencing step) has no name and contributes\n   212\t   nothing.\"\n   213\t  [ast]\n   214\t  (into #{}\n   215\t        (keep (fn [n]\n   216\t                (when (and (map? n)\n   217\t                           (= :application (:type n))\n   218\t                           (contains? n :yang/call-site))\n   219\t                  (get-in n [:operator :name]))))\n   220\t        (nodes ast)))\n   221\t\n   222\t\n   223\t(defn- application-nodes\n   224\t  [ast]\n   225\t  (filter #(and (map? %) (= :application (:type %))) (nodes ast)))\n   226\t\n   227\t\n   228\t;; =============================================================================\n   229\t;; The production trees\n   230\t;; =============================================================================\n   231\t\n   232\t(defn- source-trees\n   233\t  \"The production trees that carry no bundled prelude, as `[label ast]`:\n   234\t   every public lowering entry point this frontend answers, plus both\n   235\t   published linker module trees. `lower-transform`'s envelope member has\n   236\t   its own test, because its origin is the stage's admission, not this\n   237\t   file's.\"\n   238\t  []\n   239\t  [[\"lower-module-body\" (lower/lower-module-body var-x)]\n   240\t   [\"lower-unit\" (lower/lower-unit var-x)]\n   241\t   [\"lower-units, linked, two units\"\n   242\t    (lower/lower-units [var-x log-x] {:prelude :linked})]\n   243\t   [\"lower-units, linked, no unit\" (lower/lower-units [] {:prelude :linked})]\n   244\t   [\"lower-packet, linked\" (lower/lower-packet var-x {:prelude :linked})]\n   245\t   [\"lower-packet, linked, a loop\"\n   246\t    (lower/lower-packet while-x {:prelude :linked})]\n   247\t   [\"lower-packet, linked, a function\"\n   248\t    (lower/lower-packet function-f {:prelude :linked})]\n   249\t   [\"js module-uast\" prelude/module-uast]\n   250\t   [\"jssp module-uast\" hooks/module-uast]])\n   251\t\n   252\t\n   253\t(defn- bundled-trees\n   254\t  \"The bundled profile: the whole prelude tree composed ahead of the body,\n   255\t   so the composition — not the unit — is the finalized tree.\"\n   256\t  []\n   257\t  [[\"lower-packet, bundled\" (lower/lower-packet var-x)]\n   258\t   [\"lower-units, bundled\" (lower/lower-units [var-x log-x])]])\n   259\t\n   260\t\n   261\t(defn- cheap-trees\n   262\t  \"The trees a lane may walk repeatedly without paying for the prelude.\"\n   263\t  []\n   264\t  (remove (fn [[label _]]\n   265\t            (or (str/includes? label \"module-uast\")\n   266\t                (str/includes? label \"bundled\")))\n   267\t          (source-trees)))\n   268\t\n   269\t\n   270\t;; =============================================================================\n   271\t;; The equality gate\n   272\t;; =============================================================================\n   273\t\n   274\t(deftest equality-gate-test\n   275\t  (doseq [[label ast] (concat (source-trees) (bundled-trees))]\n   276\t    (testing label\n   277\t      (let [{:keys [tree metadata]} (project ast)]\n   278\t        (is (seq (marked metadata))\n   279\t            \"the tree claims coverage: it emits C1 rows at all\")\n   280\t        (is (= (eligible tree) (marked metadata))\n   281\t            \"the eligible application set equals the marker set\")\n   282\t        (is (= (occurrence-pairs tree) (marked-pairs metadata))\n   283\t            \"and on the origin-free projection a consumer derives alone\")\n   284\t        (is (true? (yang/validate-call-site-coverage! tree metadata origin)))\n   285\t        (is (true? (yang/validate-ast-call-sites! ast origin)))\n   286\t        (is (every? (fn [row]\n   287\t                      (and (= 5 (count row))\n   288\t                           (= origin (nth row 0))\n   289\t                           (= (:root tree) (nth row 1))\n   290\t                           (= :yang/call-site (nth row 3))\n   291\t                           (= 1 (nth row 4))))\n   292\t                    (marker-rows metadata))\n   293\t            \"every row is the core's coordinate tuple, exactly:\n   294\t             [origin root-address path :yang/call-site 1]\")\n   295\t        (is (every? #(= (:root tree) (nth % 1)) metadata)\n   296\t            \"no row of the relation names another tree\")))))\n   297\t\n   298\t\n   299\t(deftest stage-envelope-test\n   300\t  (testing \"the streaming stage's envelope carries the finalized tree under\n   301\t            the STAGE's admission origin, which the composition supplies\"\n   302\t    (doseq [profile [:bundled :linked]]\n   303\t      (testing (str profile)\n   304\t        (let [[_ [[port envelope]]] (lower/lower-transform {:prelude profile}\n   305\t                                                           var-x)\n   306\t              projected (encoder/project envelope)\n   307\t              tree (nth (:yin/batch projected) (:yin/root projected))\n   308\t              metadata (:yin/frontend-metadata projected)\n   309\t              admission (vm/source-origin lower/program-medium [:hand 0] 0)]\n   310\t          (is (= :program port))\n   311\t          (is (= admission [:source lower/program-medium [:hand 0] 0])\n   312\t              \"the packet's unit is the batch token, as the stage documents\")\n   313\t          (is (= (eligible-under tree admission) (marked-under metadata admission)))\n   314\t          (is (true? (yang/validate-call-site-coverage! tree metadata admission)))\n   315\t          (is (empty? (marked-under metadata origin))\n   316\t              \"no C1 row of the envelope carries THIS file's origin: the\n   317\t               frontend finalizes the tree and the composition admits it, so\n   318\t               the frontend stamps no origin of its own\")\n   319\t          (is (= #{admission} (into #{} (map first) (marker-rows metadata)))\n   320\t              \"and every C1 row carries exactly the stage's admission\n   321\t               origin — one origin, supplied by the composition, per the\n   322\t               design's streaming-stage inventory row: the stage supplies\n   323\t               medium plus packet unit as batch token\"))))))\n   324\t\n   325\t\n   326\t;; =============================================================================\n   327\t;; The boundary: what is an occurrence here, and what is data\n   328\t;; =============================================================================\n   329\t\n   330\t(deftest boundary-test\n   331\t  (let [linked (lower/lower-packet log-x {:prelude :linked})]\n   332\t    (testing \"every application node, and only an application node, carries the key\"\n   333\t      (is (= (count (application-nodes linked))\n   334\t             (count (filter #(= 1 (:yang/call-site %)) (application-nodes linked))))\n   335\t          \"no application occurrence is left unclaimed\")\n   336\t      (is (not-any? #(and (map? %)\n   337\t                          (contains? % :yang/call-site)\n   338\t                          (not= :application (:type %)))\n   339\t                    (nodes linked))\n   340\t          \"no lambda, literal, variable or if is marked\"))\n   341\t    (testing \"the ts frontend emits only grammar node types, so the shared\n   342\t              walk can never reach its Unknown-AST-node-type refusal\"\n   343\t      (is (every? #(contains? vm/semantic-bytecode-grammar (:type %))\n   344\t                  (filter #(and (map? %) (contains? % :type)) (nodes linked)))))\n   345\t    (testing \"a literal payload is data, never syntax: the walk does not enter it\"\n   346\t      (is (not-any? #(and (map? %)\n   347\t                          (= :literal (:type %))\n   348\t                          (some #{:yang/call-site}\n   349\t                                (tree-seq coll? seq (:value %))))\n   350\t                    (nodes linked))))\n   351\t    (testing \"the generated runtime, member and dispatch applications each\n   352\t              get their own K (design §5.3)\"\n   353\t      (is (every? (marked-operator-names linked)\n   354\t                  '[js/run-main js/call js/get-value js/global-get\n   355\t                    cell/new cell/set! require js/init!])\n   356\t          \"source calls lower to js/call over js/get-value, a free name to\n   357\t           js/global-get, a binding to cell/new + cell/set!, and the linked\n   358\t           profile's own require/init wrapper applications are occurrences\n   359\t           too — none of them escapes marking\"))\n   360\t    (testing \"an immediately applied lambda is an ordinary occurrence\"\n   361\t      (is (some #(and (= :application (:type %))\n   362\t                      (contains? % :yang/call-site)\n   363\t                      (= :lambda (:type (:operator %))))\n   364\t                (application-nodes linked))\n   365\t          \"a scope's cell binding and a sequencing step are applications\"))\n   366\t    (testing \"a published module tree's yin/def occurrences are marked\"\n   367\t      (is (contains? (marked-operator-names hooks/module-uast) 'yin/def))\n   368\t      (is (contains? (marked-operator-names prelude/module-uast) 'yin/def))\n   369\t      (is (= 1 (:yang/call-site hooks/module-uast))\n   370\t          \"the module tree's root is one wide application\"))))\n   371\t\n   372\t\n   373\t;; =============================================================================\n   374\t;; The validation failures a consumer must be able to name\n   375\t;; =============================================================================\n   376\t\n   377\t(deftest validation-failure-test\n   378\t  (let [ast (lower/lower-packet var-x {:prelude :linked})\n   379\t        {:keys [tree metadata]} (project ast)\n   380\t        markers (marker-rows metadata)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
