lives in `yang.clojure`, so a ts test depends on the clojure frontend.**\n666:  now does for the core, and record the J1-J4 rulings there.\n692:(design `:57`). J4 is filed as a *flag*, not a redesign, per the brief's instruction.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/yang-clojure/1794670000000-architect-callsite-generalization-design.gpt-6-astra.findings.md | sed -n '32,100p;125,170p'\nnl -ba test/yang/typescript_callsite_test.cljc | sed -n '686,745p'\nnl -ba /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/yang-typescript/1794514249000-engineer-ts-callsite-adoption.qwen3.8-max.findings.md | sed -n '541,605p'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/yang-clojure/1794670000000-architect-callsite-generalization-design.gpt-6-astra.findings.md | sed -n '32,100p;125,170p'\nnl -ba test/yang/typescript_callsite_test.cljc | sed -n '686,745p'\nnl -ba /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/yang-typescript/1794514249000-engineer-ts-callsite-adoption.qwen3.8-max.findings.md | sed -n '541,605p'\"","aggregated_output":"    32\t### 2.1 Identity and scope\n    33\t\n    34\tAn application site is `K = [origin root-address path]`.\n    35\t\n    36\t- `root-address` is the canonical root of the particular final UAST tree being named, not the application's subtree address or an instrumented runtime-map hash.\n    37\t- `path` is the grammar's structural path: scalar child slot steps are row positions; a child in a `nodes` slot is `[slot-position member-index]`. The root is `[]`. Never substitute map keys, host iteration order, allocation ids, source line numbers, PCs, callee names, or arities.\n    38\t- `origin` identifies the actual admission or generation event. Admitted syntax uses `[:source medium batch-token j]`; generated syntax uses `[:expansion expansion-record-address]`. Generated post-expansion trees must not be mislabeled as original source or given a fabricated expansion address. If a no-op expansion retains an admitted tree, the original source origin remains valid; “post-expansion” names the pipeline boundary, not proof that a generating event occurred.\n    39\t- An origin is supplied by the admitting/generating composition. Two separately admitted identical sources have different origins; two identical applications in one tree have different paths; two expansion attempts with identical output have different producing records. Replaying a single recorded admission is different from admitting the same text again.\n    40\t\n    41\tThe implemented origin validator accepts exactly the source and expansion shapes (`src/cljc/yin/vm.cljc:938-958`). `vm/occurrences` returns `[root path node-id]`, one per place, with origin fixed by the composition; it does not return full keys or count only distinct row ids (`vm.cljc:1589-1609`).\n    42\t\n    43\tCoverage is **every final `:application` occurrence**, including generated wrappers, adapters, dispatcher/helper calls, bundled preludes, imported preludes, recursion, and statically indirect applications. “Source call” and “attributable upstream call” are projections over this coverage, not filters that delete other occurrences. Rule R's `yin/def` is structurally an application but lowers to `:define`; it gets an occurrence annotation and never a fictitious callee-entry event (`semantic/linearize.cljc:106-116`).\n    44\t\n    45\tDedicated operations such as `:dao.stream.apply/call`, stream nodes, and continuation nodes retain existing instruction provenance. They are not silently counted as `:application` sites. Their adapters' application occurrences are covered; an extension to count other node kinds must explicitly version the coverage policy (`vm.cljc:1015-1028`; `semantic/linearize.cljc:126-139`).\n    46\t\n    47\t### 2.2 Minimal persisted annotation\n    48\t\n    49\tReserve `:yang/call-site` in the existing frontend-metadata relation:\n    50\t\n    51\t```clojure\n    52\t[origin root-address path :yang/call-site 1]\n    53\t```\n    54\t\n    55\tThe integer `1` versions this key's coverage/interpretation contract. The first three coordinates ARE the site id; the value does not repeat it. This key is distinct from existing `:yang/site`, whose meaning is safepoint marks (`src/cljc/yang/safepoint.cljc:55-75`). It carries no language name, source arity, ambient-context classification, or callee identity. Those are consumer evidence derived by the oracle or another explicitly versioned consumer.\n    56\t\n    57\tThe marker certifies that a producer preserved this occurrence under C1; the application predicate itself remains derived from canonical rows. There is no new canonical fact asserting what the grammar already says. A consumer can derive the eligible application set and compare it with the complete marker set. Under a C1 publication claim the sets must be equal; mere absence of annotations in an older publication is not false evidence of zero applications.\n    58\t\n    59\tEmit precisely one logical marker per eligible occurrence. Duplicate identical transport deliveries may be deduplicated as the same immutable fact; duplicate entries in a declared canonical table, conflicting values, unsupported versions, nonexistent paths, non-application targets, and missing/extra rows under a complete-coverage claim are validation failures. Other frontend metadata is preserved independently.\n    60\t\n    61\tImplementation may add this marker to temporary frontend map nodes before side-table projection, since the current extractor recognizes namespace `yang` (`vm.cljc:1183-1214`). Prefer deriving the relation directly from validated rows where map attachment would be redundant. `ast->semantic-bytecode` hashes only grammar slots and drops other node keys (`vm.cljc:1113-1123`); no grammar slot, instruction operand, canonical datom slot, or AST contract revision is authorized by C1.\n    62\t\n    63\t### 2.3 Finalization and transformations\n    64\t\n    65\tFinalize paths only after macro expansion, generated-name canonicalization, wrappers, module/SCC assembly, and tail marking that determine the named tree. Source-level annotations alone cannot cover generated calls (base ruling R2 at line 17). Low-level functions returning fragments may defer finalization until an owning root and origin exist; each executable/publication ingress must invoke the common finalizer. A frontend cannot claim adoption by marking just its parser or user-call lowering arm.\n    66\t\n    67\tA subsequent tree-changing transform creates another root and another occurrence relation. It must preserve an explicit old/new occurrence correspondence where it makes an attribution claim, recompute C1 for new applications, and identify generated helper calls separately. It must not retain stale paths or equate every new helper with the nearest source call. If a transform deletes, duplicates, or merges occurrences, its correspondence must record the actual multiplicity; ambiguity refuses attribution.\n    68\t\n    69\tMacro expansion already records input root, call path, macro root, parent, output and attempt (`src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc:997-1000,1062-1119`). However, final tail marking and stand-in lowering happen later (`:1255-1260`). The implementation inventory must resolve how final published roots are related to these expansion outputs. Whether the existing event/record adapters already provide the complete final-root correspondence is **unknown — the implementation round's inventory decides**. Do not assume an intermediate output record identifies every occurrence in the final assembled tree, and do not mint a fake `:expand` merely to satisfy the shape.\n    70\t\n    71\t### 2.4 Lowering, reconstruction, and runtime lookup\n    72\t\n    73\tPersist the existing instruction relation `[segment-address pc origin root-address path]`. The row linearizer already returns `{:address ... :provenance [[pc origin root path] ...]}`; its caller supplies the segment coordinate (`semantic/linearize.cljc:188-214`; code-as-tuples §5.3 at lines 918–931). A call dispatch looks up its **own call instruction's** emitting occurrence, not the preceding operand's instruction or the callee's body. Multiple instructions may belong to one occurrence.\n    74\t\n    75\tSegment+PC alone is insufficient when identical code is loaded under two origins. The runtime must retain its load/admission origin alongside its image reference when selecting provenance. This is an occurrence-scoped runtime context, not a new code hash. The native image derivations must supply or independently reconstruct a mapping from their call PCs back through semantic PCs to K; PC equality across formats must not be assumed. Current semantic `resolve` preserves PCs, register derivation preserves layout, and stack derivation emits a new sequence (`semantic/derive.cljc:21-42,60-93,154-172`).\n    76\t\n    77\tCanonical reconstruction deliberately shares nodes by content (`vm.cljc:1477-1486,1522-1525`). Never cache an occurrence annotation by node-id or mutate a shared canonical reconstruction and expect distinct sites to survive. Keep an occurrence cursor/side lookup, or expand occurrence-specific ephemeral images. The datom linearizer currently returns `[pc entity]`, not K (`semantic/linearize.cljc:283-302`); use an explicit entity-to-occurrence bridge with the owning batch, root and path, refusing ambiguity. `encoder/datom-entity-occurrences` and the envelope's `:yin/entity-occurrences` are the starting machinery (`encoder.cljc:67,115-148`).\n    78\t\n    79\t### 2.5 Ephemeral origin and trace field\n    80\t\n    81\tName the nonpersistent domain **ephemeral instrumentation origin**. Its C1 spelling is:\n    82\t\n    83\t```clojure\n    84\t[:ephemeral evidence-scope-token compilation-token member-index]\n    85\t;; ephemeral site:\n    86\t[ephemeral-origin canonical-compiled-root structural-path]\n    87\t;; already signed trace shape:\n    88\t[fname arity caller-site-id]\n    89\t```\n    90\t\n    91\tThe composition supplies two non-nil plain-data tokens: `evidence-scope-token` names the recording/fixture scope; `compilation-token` names this particular instrumented compilation in that scope. `member-index` is a nonnegative integer. They are explicitly recorded inputs, not inferred from source hash, host object identity, time, lane name, or callee. Both oracle C lanes execute the SAME compiled artifact with the same tokens; a separate compilation gets another token. Replay uses the recorded tokens. A source hash alone would collapse distinct attempts.\n    92\t\n    93\tThis is a precise proposed spelling for the still-unfrozen oracle implementation. It is **not** a third legal persisted occurrence origin: `vm/occurrence-origin?` must continue rejecting it. An EDN evidence file may preserve an ephemeral id as evidence of that run; that does not convert it into a portable code occurrence. Persisted C1 side tables and expansion links require real ruled origins.\n    94\t\n    95\tThe canonical compiled root is computed after code-producing instrumentation that changes the AST, before occurrence stamps are associated into runtime maps. Runtime stamping must not introduce a root-hash self-reference. If instrumentation subsequently changes structure, it must carry an explicit transform mapping or recompute the frozen site table; no path can silently retain its old meaning.\n    96\t\n    97\tThe oracle must finalize the spelling in its own versioned evidence contract and use that format once. If its accepted schema differs by the time implementation starts, preserve its evidence verbatim and publish a reviewed binding of its origin fields to this semantic domain; do not rewrite its tables behind an unchanged version. A semantic conflict (no compilation scope, map-key paths, callee ids) requires correction on the oracle's record, not a silent normalization in durable verification.\n    98\t\n    99\tRuntime `assoc` stamping is explicitly licensed by §2.6, owner ruling 2026-09-15: the walker holds an ephemeral image and nothing runtime-associated is projected back to canonical rows; runtime keys must be stripped at serialization/projection of continuation frames (`docs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:459-474`). Static frontend marker extraction is a separate, pre-execution side-table operation. This clause licenses oracle-specific walker instrumentation; it does not establish ordinary production coverage.\n   100\t\n   125\t\n   126\tWhether some existing higher-level ledger/publication mechanism can carry this new correspondence without **its own** schema change is **unknown — the implementation round's inventory decides**. The narrower question is answered: the inspected linker's `record-defect` cannot accept extra keys under today's `:yin.ledger/record`. This design avoids making that compatibility claim.\n   127\t\n   128\t### 3.2 Producer-to-consumer preservation inventory\n   129\t\n   130\t| Surface and inspected locations | Required implementation work / read-only dependency |\n   131\t|---|---|\n   132\t| Clojure `compile-form`, `compile`, `compile-program`, `lower-unit`: `src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:2021,2164,2839,2993` | Cover native and argument-vector/outcome compilation, library/adapters, linked unit wrapping and global publication. Finalize at executable roots, after expansion. Existing fragment APIs need not invent origins. |\n   133\t| TypeScript packet/body/unit/multi-unit/stage: `yang/typescript/antlr/lower.cljc:2262-2363` | Cover bundled and linked runtime paths, canonical names and tail marks, all units and generated runtime calls. Preserve packet/source association separately. |\n   134\t| PHP ANTLR body/program/packet/module/SCC/stage: `yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc:3737,3759,3800,3840,3855,3929,3998-4041` | Cover includes, class-map units, strict-types variants, SCC bundles/aliases, helpers and linked/bundled paths. |\n   135\t| Legacy PHP `compile-program/compile`: `yang/php.cljc:640-685` | Additional live frontend, not retired by the presence of ANTLR. Annotate all generated combinator/wrapper applications too. |\n   136\t| Python module/body/packet/SCC/stage: `yang/python/antlr/lower.cljc:2018,2030,2097,2139,2198,2298,2334-2373`; session `repl.cljc:86-108` | Cover stateless and already-primed sessions, imports, bundles/aliases and generated body wrappers; first-session prelude coverage cannot stand in for subsequent submissions. |\n   137\t| REPL frontend catalog: `yin/repl/frontends.cljc:24-110` | Covers single-form vs multi-form Clojure, legacy PHP, Python session lowering and Jolt native parser selection. Standard catalog does not currently register TypeScript; direct TS paths still require adoption. |\n   138\t| Common UAST/prelude/call/module emitters: `yang/core/prelude.cljc:44-69,138-159`, `yang/core/call.cljc:184-191`, `yang/core/module.cljc:31-99` | These produce wrapper/helper/prelude code outside source-call arms. Apply common finalization at the owning publication, including direct hand-built UAST accepted as frontend output. |\n   139\t| Common streaming stage: `yang/core/stage.cljc:25-59` | It currently supplies medium plus packet unit as batch token. Audit distinct re-admissions of the same unit: C1 requires fresh admission identity while retry keeps the token; packet identity alone is insufficient if reused for distinct admissions. |\n   140\t| Encoder map/rows/datoms: `yin/vm/encoder.cljc:25-43,67-148,230-258` | Map projection emits side tables; already-projected rows currently return empty tables; envelope projection replaces table fields. Preserve/validate supplied metadata and finalize generated output instead of silently dropping it. Maintain batch member j. |\n   141\t| Macro pipeline: `yin/vm/macro.cljc:997-1005,1062-1119,1196-1261` | Keep expansion attempt provenance, resolve final-root ownership, annotate generated occurrences and retain retrievable expansion records. Post-expansion is a required integration point. |\n   142\t| Safepoint insertion: `yang/safepoint.cljc:234-256` | Current derived envelope explicitly clears frontend metadata, source positions and entity occurrences. New root needs fresh C1 plus verified input/output mapping; preserve the safepoint record's separate semantics. |\n   143\t| Projection and row validation: `yin/vm.cljc:1113-1159,1217-1259,1262-1456,1589-1609` | Reuse grammar traversal, plain-data checks and occurrence enumeration. Add a side-table coverage validator, not C1 requirements to canonical row validation. Unannotated legacy rows remain valid. |\n   144\t| Canonical and datom reconstruction: `yin/vm.cljc:705,818-851,1477-1555` | Side metadata does not reappear from content alone. Attach provenance context out of band; do not collapse occurrence ids via shared reconstruction/entity ids. Round-trip canonical hashes must remain equal. |\n   145\t| Semantic row and datom lowering: `yin/vm/semantic/linearize.cljc:106-128,188-221,283-302` | Persist returned provenance, supply origins explicitly, bridge datom entities with occurrences; nil-origin legacy calls remain loadable but cannot satisfy C1 attribution. |\n   146\t| Native lowering: `yin/vm/semantic/derive.cljc:21-42,60-120,154-184` | Produce/reconstruct complete native-call-PC provenance; compose with semantic mapping. Sparse variable/closure diagnostics do not establish call coverage. Inventory any legacy direct de Bruijn lowering still reached after merges. |\n   147\t| Runtime dispatch and resume: `yin/vm/ast_walker.cljc:273-332,493,625-711,776`; `yin/vm/semantic.cljc:102,142,333-380` | Cold/hot application routes, operator/operand frames, linked image attachment and resumption all need occurrence context for traced execution. Native engines and UCF lifting must be audited too; no claim they already preserve caller K. |\n   148\t| Existing derivation verification: `yin/vm/ledger.cljc:156-215`, `yin/vm/linker.cljc:2164-2255` | Existing verification re-lowers code and compares identities, not side metadata. Keep code verification and add independent provenance/correspondence verification. `:trusted` does not satisfy this new acceptance gate. |\n   149\t| Generic publication: `yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc:115-218` | Currently takes only `:vector` from `project-rows` at line 157. Publish complete side artifacts and origin/record closure beside code; do not discard provenance or change manifest keys casually. Validate before making a C1 availability claim. |\n   150\t| Unit publication: `yang/core/publication.cljc:92-170`, PHP `publication.cljc:27-70`, Python `publication.cljc:27-80` | Publish records for actual bundle roots; aliases cannot borrow unrelated paths. Coordinate side artifacts with index/discovery publication. PHP currently has nil site-set/binder hooks; Python's site-set hook is safepoint-specific. |\n   151\t| Site-set discovery/signing precedent: `yang/python/antlr/siteset.cljc:5-31,65-101` | Reuse the separate-record-by-manifest pattern and declared-principal verification where appropriate. Its exact key schema is not the caller-site or oracle schema. Inventory discovery/fetch/retention paths for the new record explicitly. |\n   152\t| Code index / republishing: `yin/repl/ast_index.cljc:3-24,108`; `yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc:225-300` | Query views can be rebuilt from rows but cannot recover omitted admission provenance. Session/index-to-module publication must preserve or explicitly remap occurrence roots, and retain original evidence sources. |\n   153\t| Oracle instrumentation/accounting: `test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:1786-1855,2341-2405,2432-2468` | Oracle-owned trace migration, offset retirement across the full family, both lanes, refusal pins, gate accounting and evidence regeneration per R5/R6. Audit table derivation independently per R7. |\n   154\t\n   155\t### 3.3 Persisted artifacts and publication blast radius\n   156\t\n   157\t“Side tables are additive” is the compatibility policy, not permission to skip republishing coverage evidence. **Unannotated persisted artifacts remain loadable under their supported existing code contracts.** A provenance-requiring query returns missing provenance/refuses credit; it never invents identity from names, hashes, arities, values or source lines. Old provenance may be reconstructed only when the actual admission/expansion inputs are retained, and the result is a newly verified artifact.\n   158\t\n   159\tThe implementation inventory must enumerate, regenerate where changed, and verify these families on **all four host lanes**:\n   160\t\n   161\t1. `yang.call`, Clojure `clj` and its library, TypeScript `js/jssp`, Python `py/pysp`, and PHP `php` plus its hook/runtime publications. Shared emitter anchors: `yang/core/call.cljc:184`, `yang/clojure/prelude.cljc:125-143`, TS `prelude.cljc:4168-4260`, Python `prelude.cljc:3645-3739`, PHP `prelude.cljc:5328-5411`. Include PHP's definition lists `prelude_module.cljc:386` and `prelude_p9.cljc:558`; their inclusion must not escape measurement because they are emitted through the main prelude.\n   162\t2. For each host publication: canonical row closure, semantic vector, stack/register stored images and checksums, derivation records, schema-1 manifest, pinned dependency addresses, new C1 side tables/provenance/correspondence, and discovery/index/name/signature records where used. The actual publication sequence is `yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc:156-209`. Side-only annotation should leave old code addresses unchanged; measure this rather than assume it. New side objects still need publication, retrieval and retention.\n   163\t3. Fresh process-local prelude caches, linked harnesses and golden addresses: TS `test/yang/typescript/antlr/linked_harness.cljc:55-78`, Python `test/yang/python/antlr/linked_harness.cljc:55-77`, PHP `test/yang/php/antlr/linked_harness.cljc:38-56`. Reusing a realized pre-change delay is not a republication test.\n   164\t4. Imported user modules, SCC bundles and aliases, class maps, safepointed derivatives, session/module exports, signed discovery entries and DHT fixtures. Specifically `test/resources/yang/python/dht-import-v1.edn` and its generator `dht-import-v1.generate.clj:1-20`, which says to regenerate whenever lowering/publication/prelude changes addresses. Preserve old fixtures as compatibility inputs where practical, rather than rewriting away the only legacy-load test.\n   165\t5. Oracle evidence: new versioned caller-site tables; `slice9_evidence.edn`, `slice9_verification.edn`, `slice9_declarations.edn`, `slice9_unexercised.edn`, `fixture_closure.edn`, gate markdown and captured verification/test outputs; `context.edn`, `kernel_gate.edn`, `manifest.edn` and earlier slice evidence as input/history or regeneration targets according to actual dependency. Every changed trace-bearing field/pin must be listed; blanket rewriting of historical evidence is not required.\n   166\t6. Explicitly inventory `test/yang/latte_oracle/throw_sites.edn:1-7` and `case_arms.edn:1-11`. They currently contain bare vectors of source inventory maps, with no top-level schema stamp. Their producer is `src/dev/latte_oracle_tables.clj:15-24,52-64`; throw-site equality checking is `latte_oracle_test.clj:679-699`. They are **read/validated unchanged** if their meaning/shape remains unchanged. If caller-site coordinates or new fields are added, version their evidence contract and update producer, validator, readers, generators and pins together. They are not automatically the R1 versioned application-site table, and source `:line` is not K.\n   167\t\n   168\tThe addendum names TypeScript `publication.cljc`, but no `src/cljc/yang/typescript/antlr/publication.cljc` exists in the inspected checkout. TS prelude publication is presently visible in its linked harness above; its design describes later publication work (`docs/design/yang.typescript.md:1347,1545`). Whether an in-flight seat supplies a new file, renamed path, or equivalent hook is **unknown — the implementation round's inventory decides**. It remains a named mandatory inventory item, not a silent omission or an invented present file.\n   169\t\n   170\t### 3.4 Failure separation\n   686\t;; =============================================================================\n   687\t;; The export audit (the python F2 pin's shape, itself the ts twin's mirror)\n   688\t;; =============================================================================\n   689\t\n   690\t(deftest export-audit-pin-test\n   691\t  (testing \"no C1 or exception-track provenance surface is guest-visible\"\n   692\t    (let [exposed? (fn [x]\n   693\t                     (some #(str/includes? (str x) %)\n   694\t                           [\"call-site\" \"callsite\" \"call_site\"\n   695\t                            \"dsg__\" \"provenance\"]))]\n   696\t      (doseq [[label exports runtime-keys]\n   697\t              [[\"js\" prelude/module-exports prelude/runtime-keys]\n   698\t               [\"jssp\" hooks/module-exports hooks/runtime-keys]]]\n   699\t        (testing label\n   700\t          (is (not-any? exposed? exports)\n   701\t              \"no export names the occurrence contract or the runtime doors\")\n   702\t          (is (not-any? exposed? runtime-keys)\n   703\t              \"no runtime key the task allocates names either\")))))\n   704\t  (testing \"no js definition reaches the exception track's reserved doors,\n   705\t            and none carries the compile-time C1 key\"\n   706\t    (let [private-names '#{cell/dsg__new-provenance\n   707\t                           cell/dsg__provenance\n   708\t                           dsg__condition-exception}\n   709\t          door-users (into #{}\n   710\t                           (keep (fn [[k form]]\n   711\t                                   (when (some private-names\n   712\t                                               (tree-seq coll? seq form))\n   713\t                                     k)))\n   714\t                           prelude/definitions)\n   715\t          c1-users (into #{}\n   716\t                         (keep (fn [[k form]]\n   717\t                                 (when (some #{:yang/call-site}\n   718\t                                             (tree-seq coll? seq form))\n   719\t                                   k)))\n   720\t                         prelude/definitions)]\n   721\t      (is (= #{} door-users)\n   722\t          \"a DIFFERENT key family: the js prelude authenticates a retained\n   723\t           condition through its own sealed companion cell, never the VM's\n   724\t           provenance doors, so nothing here re-mints or reuses them\")\n   725\t      (is (= #{} c1-users)\n   726\t          \"C1 is compile-time frontend metadata on the lowered tree, never\n   727\t           a guest definition the runtime can read\")))\n   728\t  (testing \"the audited surface is the whole guest-visible surface, not a\n   729\t            sample of it\"\n   730\t    (is (= (set prelude/module-exports)\n   731\t           (into #{}\n   732\t                 (keep (fn [[k _]]\n   733\t                         (when (= \"js\" (namespace k)) (prelude/strip k))))\n   734\t                 prelude/definitions))\n   735\t        \"the js exports are exactly its js-namespaced definitions; the\n   736\t         internal js.rt/* store keys are not exported\")\n   737\t    (is (= (set hooks/module-exports)\n   738\t           (set (map (comp hooks/strip first) hooks/function-definitions)))\n   739\t        \"and jssp's are exactly its definition list, mirroring\n   740\t         linked-prelude-test's own pin\")))\n   541\t## 7. The four judgement calls needing the orchestrator's ruling\n   542\t\n   543\t**J1 — Is `jssp` in scope? I marked it.**\n   544\t`safepoint.cljc:186-197` now finalizes the `jssp` module tree. Grounds: design `:278` says\n   545\t\"Cover … bundled and linked `js`, `yang.call`, **and safepoint runtime**\", and `:161`'s\n   546\tpersisted-artifact family 1 names \"TypeScript **`js/jssp`**\". `jssp` is genuinely published\n   547\ton a production path (`linked_harness.cljc:70-78`, witnessed by\n   548\t`linked_prelude_test.cljc:153-157`), so leaving it unmarked would leave a published\n   549\tproduction module without C1 — a coverage gap acceptance would find. Cost: it broke one\n   550\tassertion (`linked_prelude_test.cljc:61-63`), repaired in §1.2.\n   551\t**If you instead read \"safepoint runtime\" as the hook-insertion *stage* rather than the\n   552\tpublished `jssp` module, revert `safepoint.cljc:186-197` AND\n   553\t`linked_prelude_test.cljc:61-63` together** — reverting one without the other breaks the test.\n   554\t\n   555\t**J2 — The bundled composition fragments are not marked at their own `def`.**\n   556\t`prelude/uast`, `prelude/functions-uast`, `hooks/uast`, `hooks/noop-uast`, `hooks/program`,\n   557\t`hooks/linked-program` stay unmarked as standalone vars; they are finalized only as part of\n   558\tthe tree the owning publication produces (§2.2), per design `:138` (\"Apply common\n   559\tfinalization at the **owning publication**\"). **The risk if you rule the other way:** marking\n   560\tthe fragments at their `def` makes every host that composes a fragment with an unmarked tree\n   561\t— `e2e_test.clj:112-116` (`hooks/program` over a row-round-tripped derived AST),\n   562\t`safepoint_test.clj`, `source_call_test.cljc:57-63` — produce a **partially** marked tree,\n   563\twhich is a false claim at any publication or batch boundary and is refused outright by\n   564\t`publish-module!`. **The risk of my choice:** if any host publishes `prelude/uast` directly\n   565\tas frontend output rather than composing it through `lower-packet`, that publication is\n   566\tunclaimed. I found no such host in this worktree — the only direct consumers are\n   567\t`lower.cljc:2284` (`with-runtime`) and the float/prelude tests. Ruling requested: confirm\n   568\t\"owning publication\" is the right seam for ts, or name the fragment that must self-finalize.\n   569\t\n   570\t**J3 — No `:injected-origin` for the safepoint stage's injected hook applications.**\n   571\tAfter this round a derived ts envelope carries C1 rows covering only the **surviving**\n   572\toccurrences; the injected `js.sp/loop` / `jssp/loop` applications are recorded in\n   573\t`:correspondence` as `{:kind :safepoint/injected :path p}` with **no origin**, so the derived\n   574\ttable is not a complete-coverage claim (§4.4). I did not supply one, because\n   575\t`yang/safepoint.cljc` is outside my surface bounds, the origin belongs to the *admitting\n   576\tcomposition* and not to a frontend, and inventing one is exactly what design `:69` forbids\n   577\t(*\"do not mint a fake `:expand` merely to satisfy the shape\"*). The clojure-side precedent\n   578\tfor supplying one is `clojure_callsite_test.cljc:1355-1457` (`sp-injected-origin`).\n   579\t**Ruling requested:** should the ts safepoint path supply an admission origin (and if so, who\n   580\towns minting it — the stage, the host, or the REPL catalog entry ts does not yet have), or is\n   581\t\"derived tree's C1 coverage is intentionally partial\" the accepted contract? Until that is\n   582\tsettled, no ts host may re-project a derived envelope through `encoder/project`.\n   583\t\n   584\t**J4 — The C1 validator lives in `yang.clojure`, so a ts test depends on the clojure frontend.**\n   585\t`yang/core/uast.cljc:126-128` states: *\"The walk lives here, beside the other shared tree\n   586\ttransforms, so every frontend's module trees finalize the same way; **`yang.clojure` owns the\n   587\tcontract's validation over canonical rows**.\"* I therefore call\n   588\t`yang/validate-call-site-coverage!` and `yang/validate-ast-call-sites!` rather than\n   589\treimplementing them — reimplementing would be precisely the \"parallel mechanism\" the brief\n   590\tforbids. `yang.clojure` is genuinely portable (`.cljc`; its docstring says *\"written in .cljc\n   591\tformat to run on both JVM and Node.js\"*; its ns form carries\n   592\t`#?@(:jolt [] :cljd [] :clj […] :cljs […])` reader conditionals at `:29-40`) and the\n   593\tdependency is light (`dao.jing`, `yang.core.call`, `yang.core.uast`, `yin.vm`), with\n   594\t`test/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc` as precedent. But **php and python will each inherit\n   595\tthe same cross-frontend dependency.** Ruling requested: authorize a follow-up lift of\n   596\t`validate-call-site-coverage!` / `validate-ast-call-sites!` / `call-site-metadata` /\n   597\t`eligible-application-sites` / `marked-application-sites` into `yang.core` (a core change, so\n   598\ta STOP-and-report for me, not something I did), so three frontends are not all requiring a\n   599\tfourth's namespace to validate a language-neutral contract.\n   600\t\n   601\t---\n   602\t\n   603\t## 8. Three citation notes on the brief itself\n   604\t\n   605\t**C1 — the cited design path does not exist.** The brief's line 20 points at\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"agent_message","text":"The stage repair is consistent with the design: both profiles need complete markers, with the composition supplying the admission origin. I found a separate weakness in the export audit: it compares two live surfaces, so a wrapper renamed consistently in both could pass. I’m checking the safepoint path to determine whether its partial coverage is an accepted refusal or an adoption gap.\n"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yang/core/uast.cljc | sed -n '1,220p'\nnl -ba src/cljc/yang/typescript/antlr/lower.cljc | sed -n '2190,2420p'\nnl -ba src/cljc/yang/typescript/antlr/safepoint.cljc | sed -n '1,255p'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yang/core/uast.cljc | sed -n '1,220p'\nnl -ba src/cljc/yang/typescript/antlr/lower.cljc | sed -n '2190,2420p'\nnl -ba src/cljc/yang/typescript/antlr/safepoint.cljc | sed -n '1,255p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t(ns yang.core.uast\n     2\t  \"Universal AST constructors shared by every language lowering and prelude. Every\n     3\t   function returns a canonical map node (`:literal`, `:variable`, `:lambda`,\n     4\t   `:application`, `:if`, `:vm/current-continuation`); nothing here adds a\n     5\t   node type.\n     6\t\n     7\t   `sexp->uast` reads a small s-expression notation into those same nodes so\n     8\t   the prelude can be written legibly:\n     9\t\n    10\t     symbol            -> :variable\n    11\t     (fn [params] b)   -> :lambda\n    12\t     (if t c a)        -> :if\n    13\t     (do a b ... z)    -> sequencing through one-parameter lambdas\n    14\t     (let [x v ...] b) -> nested immediately applied lambdas\n    15\t     (quote x)         -> :literal x\n    16\t     (%capture)        -> :vm/current-continuation\n    17\t     (yin/def k v)     -> the definition application\n    18\t     (f a ...)         -> :application\n    19\t     any other value   -> :literal\"\n    20\t  (:require\n    21\t    [yang.tails :as tails]\n    22\t    [yin.vm :as vm]))\n    23\t\n    24\t\n    25\t(defn lit\n    26\t  [x]\n    27\t  {:type :literal, :value x})\n    28\t\n    29\t\n    30\t(defn v\n    31\t  [sym]\n    32\t  {:type :variable, :name sym})\n    33\t\n    34\t\n    35\t(defn lam\n    36\t  [params body]\n    37\t  {:type :lambda, :params (vec params), :body body})\n    38\t\n    39\t\n    40\t(defn app\n    41\t  [op & args]\n    42\t  {:type :application, :operator op, :operands (vec args)})\n    43\t\n    44\t\n    45\t(defn if-node\n    46\t  [t c a]\n    47\t  {:type :if, :test t, :consequent c, :alternate a})\n    48\t\n    49\t\n    50\t(def capture {:type :vm/current-continuation})\n    51\t\n    52\t\n    53\t(defn def!\n    54\t  \"`(yin/def key value)`: key is a literal symbol.\"\n    55\t  [key value]\n    56\t  (app (v 'yin/def) (lit key) value))\n    57\t\n    58\t\n    59\t(def discard\n    60\t  \"The parameter a sequencing lambda binds and ignores. `%` cannot begin a\n    61\t   Python identifier, so it never shadows a guest name.\"\n    62\t  '%_)\n    63\t\n    64\t\n    65\t(defn then\n    66\t  \"Evaluate `a` for effect, then `b`.\"\n    67\t  [a b]\n    68\t  (app (lam [discard] b) a))\n    69\t\n    70\t\n    71\t(defn seq-nodes\n    72\t  \"Evaluate every node in order; the value is the last one's.\"\n    73\t  [nodes]\n    74\t  (reduce (fn [acc node] (then acc node)) (first nodes) (rest nodes)))\n    75\t\n    76\t\n    77\t(defn let1\n    78\t  [sym value body]\n    79\t  (app (lam [sym] body) value))\n    80\t\n    81\t\n    82\t(defn sexp->uast\n    83\t  [form]\n    84\t  (cond\n    85\t    (symbol? form) (v form)\n    86\t    (seq? form)\n    87\t    (let [[head & args] form]\n    88\t      (case head\n    89\t        fn (lam (first args) (sexp->uast (second args)))\n    90\t        if (if-node (sexp->uast (first args))\n    91\t                    (sexp->uast (second args))\n    92\t                    (sexp->uast (nth args 2)))\n    93\t        do (seq-nodes (map sexp->uast args))\n    94\t        let (let [[bindings body] args]\n    95\t              (reduce (fn [inner [sym value]]\n    96\t                        (let1 sym (sexp->uast value) inner))\n    97\t                      (sexp->uast body)\n    98\t                      (reverse (partition 2 bindings))))\n    99\t        quote (lit (first args))\n   100\t        %capture capture\n   101\t        (apply app (sexp->uast head) (map sexp->uast args))))\n   102\t    :else (lit form)))\n   103\t\n   104\t\n   105\t(def mark-tails\n   106\t  \"`yang.tails/mark-tails`: the lowering marks its tree with the same\n   107\t   function a rewriting stage recomputes the marks with.\"\n   108\t  tails/mark-tails)\n   109\t\n   110\t\n   111\t;; =============================================================================\n   112\t;; Call-site occurrence contract C1 (Addendum A, design §2)\n   113\t;; =============================================================================\n   114\t;;\n   115\t;; Every final `:application` occurrence of a produced tree carries the\n   116\t;; reserved frontend-metadata key `:yang/call-site` with version value `1`\n   117\t;; as a plain node key. Projection (`yin.vm/ast-side-tables`) drops the key\n   118\t;; from canonical rows and emits it into the frontend-metadata side table\n   119\t;; as `[origin root-address path :yang/call-site 1]`, where the first\n   120\t;; three coordinates are the site id. The key carries no callee identity,\n   121\t;; source arity, or ambient classification. It is distinct from\n   122\t;; `:yang/site`, the safepoint mark, which travels as node metadata.\n   123\t;; Dedicated node kinds (`:dao.stream.apply/call`, stream and\n   124\t;; continuation nodes) are not `:application` nodes and are never marked.\n   125\t;; The walk lives here, beside the other shared tree transforms, so every\n   126\t;; frontend's module trees finalize the same way; `yang.clojure` owns the\n   127\t;; contract's validation over canonical rows.\n   128\t\n   129\t(defn annotate-call-sites\n   130\t  \"The finished map AST `node` with `:yang/call-site 1` on every\n   131\t   `:application` node, at every depth the row grammar knows. Literal\n   132\t   payloads are data, never syntax, and are not walked. Marking is\n   133\t   idempotent and preserves node metadata and every other key, so\n   134\t   canonical rows, roots, and executable outcomes are unchanged.\"\n   135\t  [node]\n   136\t  (let [tag (:type node)\n   137\t        slots (get vm/semantic-bytecode-grammar tag)]\n   138\t    (when-not slots\n   139\t      (throw (ex-info \"Unknown AST node type\" {:type tag, :node node})))\n   140\t    (let [walked (reduce (fn [n [field kind]]\n   141\t                           (case kind\n   142\t                             :node (update n field annotate-call-sites)\n   143\t                             :nodes (update n field\n   144\t                                            (fn [children]\n   145\t                                              (mapv annotate-call-sites\n   146\t                                                    children)))\n   147\t                             n))\n   148\t                         node\n   149\t                         slots)]\n   150\t      (cond-> walked\n   151\t        (= :application tag) (assoc :yang/call-site 1)))))\n  2190\t                   (lower-block ctx (first (rules ctx fin \"block\")))))\n  2191\t      guarded)))\n  2192\t\n  2193\t\n  2194\t(defn- lower-stmt\n  2195\t  \"The node of `statement` `st`.\"\n  2196\t  [ctx st]\n  2197\t  (let [labels (:pending-labels ctx)\n  2198\t        ctx (dissoc ctx :pending-labels)\n  2199\t        n (first (rule-kids ctx st))]\n  2200\t    (when (token-kid ctx st \"export\") (refuse! st \"module syntax\" :T7))\n  2201\t    (case (:rule n)\n  2202\t      \"block\" (lower-block ctx n)\n  2203\t      \"variableStatement\" (lower-var ctx n)\n  2204\t      \"enumDeclaration\" (lower-enum ctx n)\n  2205\t      \"emptyStatement_\" undefined\n  2206\t      \"expressionStatement\" (lower-seq ctx (first (rules ctx n \"expressionSequence\")))\n  2207\t      \"ifStatement\" (lower-if ctx n)\n  2208\t      \"iterationStatement\" (lower-iteration ctx n labels)\n  2209\t      \"continueStatement\" (lower-jump ctx n)\n  2210\t      \"breakStatement\" (lower-jump ctx n)\n  2211\t      \"returnStatement\" (lower-return ctx n)\n  2212\t      \"labelledStatement\" (lower-labelled ctx n)\n  2213\t      \"switchStatement\" (lower-switch ctx n)\n  2214\t      \"throwStatement\" (app* 'js/throw (lower-seq ctx (first (rules ctx n \"expressionSequence\"))))\n  2215\t      \"tryStatement\" (lower-try ctx n)\n  2216\t      \"debuggerStatement\" undefined\n  2217\t      ;; hoisted to its scope's entry\n  2218\t      \"functionDeclaration\" undefined\n  2219\t      \"classDeclaration\" (let [nm (text-of ctx (first (rules ctx n \"identifier\")))]\n  2220\t                           (init-name nm (lower-class ctx n nm)))\n  2221\t      \"arrowFunctionDeclaration\" (function-value ctx n n \"\")\n  2222\t      (default-arm n))))\n  2223\t\n  2224\t\n  2225\t;; =============================================================================\n  2226\t;; Packets\n  2227\t;; =============================================================================\n  2228\t\n  2229\t(defn- context\n  2230\t  [packet]\n  2231\t  (let [pk (p/validate! packet {:diagnostic-ns diagnostic-ns})\n  2232\t        analysis (scope/analyze pk)]\n  2233\t    {:pk pk,\n  2234\t     :analysis analysis,\n  2235\t     :scope (:module analysis),\n  2236\t     :this (gen \"this\" (p/root pk)),\n  2237\t     :ret nil,\n  2238\t     :loop nil,\n  2239\t     :labels {},\n  2240\t     :pending-labels nil,\n  2241\t     :gen nil,\n  2242\t     :async nil,\n  2243\t     :class nil,\n  2244\t     :this-cell nil,\n  2245\t     :nt :undefined,\n  2246\t     :home nil,\n  2247\t     :class-cell nil,\n  2248\t     :privates {}}))\n  2249\t\n  2250\t\n  2251\t(defn- module-body\n  2252\t  [ctx]\n  2253\t  (let [root (p/root (:pk ctx))\n  2254\t        s (scope-of ctx root)\n  2255\t        stmts (statements-of ctx root)]\n  2256\t    (bind-cells (let [{:keys [vars tdz-names]} (binding-names s)]\n  2257\t                  (vec (concat (map (fn [nm] [nm undefined]) vars)\n  2258\t                               (map (fn [nm] [nm tdz]) tdz-names))))\n  2259\t                (seq-of (lower-stmts ctx stmts)))))\n  2260\t\n  2261\t\n  2262\t;; =============================================================================\n  2263\t;; Call-site occurrence contract C1 (Addendum A, design §2)\n  2264\t;; =============================================================================\n  2265\t;;\n  2266\t;; Every final `:application` occurrence of a tree this namespace answers\n  2267\t;; carries the reserved frontend-metadata key `:yang/call-site` with\n  2268\t;; version value `1` as a plain node key. Projection\n  2269\t;; (`yin.vm/ast-side-tables`) drops the key from canonical rows and emits\n  2270\t;; it into the EXISTING generic frontend-metadata side table as\n  2271\t;; `[origin root-address path :yang/call-site 1]`, so provenance stays out\n  2272\t;; of hashed content: canonical rows, roots, image addresses and\n  2273\t;; executable outcomes are unchanged. The walk itself is\n  2274\t;; `yang.core.uast/annotate-call-sites`; nothing here re-mints the key or\n  2275\t;; the coordinate tuple. It is a distinct key from `:yang/site`, the\n  2276\t;; safepoint mark, which travels as node metadata, and a distinct key\n  2277\t;; FAMILY again from the exception track's runtime provenance doors\n  2278\t;; `cell/dsg__new-provenance` / `cell/dsg__provenance`.\n  2279\t;;\n  2280\t;; Coverage is all-or-nothing: `yin.vm.encoder/program-batch` and\n  2281\t;; `yin.vm.linker.publish/publish-module!` each refuse a tree whose\n  2282\t;; markers do not exactly cover its eligible application occurrences. So\n  2283\t;; each PUBLIC entry point below finalizes once, over its own complete\n  2284\t;; tree, after canonical renaming and tail marking have settled it — and\n  2285\t;; the private `lower-unit*` seam exists so `lower-units` and\n  2286\t;; `lower-packet` compose unmarked units and walk the composed result a\n  2287\t;; single time, rather than leaving their own wrapper applications\n  2288\t;; (`js/run-main`, the two `require`s, `js/init!`, the sequencing lambdas)\n  2289\t;; unclaimed beside a marked unit.\n  2290\t\n  2291\t(defn lower-module-body\n  2292\t  \"The module's statements as one node, before the runtime wrapper: what\n  2293\t   lowering goldens compare. C1 finalized, like every tree this namespace\n  2294\t   answers.\"\n  2295\t  [packet]\n  2296\t  (u/annotate-call-sites (module-body (context packet))))\n  2297\t\n  2298\t\n  2299\t(defn- lower-unit*\n  2300\t  \"`lower-unit` before C1 finalization: the seam `lower-units` and\n  2301\t   `lower-packet` compose, so each of them finalizes once over its own\n  2302\t   complete tree.\"\n  2303\t  [packet]\n  2304\t  (let [ctx (context packet)]\n  2305\t    (u/lam [(:this ctx)] (module-body ctx))))\n  2306\t\n  2307\t\n  2308\t(defn lower-unit\n  2309\t  \"One separately scoped module body as a function of its shared global\n  2310\t   receiver. Keeping this seam lets a host compose independently parsed\n  2311\t   units without concatenating source or reinitializing the runtime.\n  2312\t   C1 finalized.\"\n  2313\t  [packet]\n  2314\t  (u/annotate-call-sites (lower-unit* packet)))\n  2315\t\n  2316\t\n  2317\t(defn- with-runtime\n  2318\t  \"Both source entry points install the shared convention before JS.\"\n  2319\t  [prelude main]\n  2320\t  (u/mark-tails\n  2321\t    (case prelude\n  2322\t      :bundled (u/then prelude/uast main)\n  2323\t      :linked (u/seq-nodes [(app* 'require (u/lit 'yang.call))\n  2324\t                            (app* 'require (u/lit prelude/module-name))\n  2325\t                            (app* 'js/init!)\n  2326\t                            main]))))\n  2327\t\n  2328\t\n  2329\t(defn lower-units\n  2330\t  \"A complete program for multiple separately parsed units. The runtime is\n  2331\t   installed and initialized once; each unit receives its own lexical body\n  2332\t   while sharing the same global object and output stream. C1 finalized\n  2333\t   once, over the composed tree.\"\n  2334\t  ([packets] (lower-units packets {}))\n  2335\t  ([packets {:keys [prelude], :or {prelude :bundled}}]\n  2336\t   (let [units (mapv lower-unit* packets)\n  2337\t         main (names/canonicalize\n  2338\t                (app* 'js/run-main\n  2339\t                      (u/lam ['this]\n  2340\t                             (if (seq units)\n  2341\t                               (u/seq-nodes\n  2342\t                                 (mapv (fn [unit] (u/app unit (u/v 'this))) units))\n  2343\t                               (u/lit :js/undefined)))))]\n  2344\t     (u/annotate-call-sites (with-runtime prelude main)))))\n  2345\t\n  2346\t\n  2347\t(defn lower-packet\n  2348\t  \"The complete program for one ok packet: the module body run by\n  2349\t   `js/run-main`, generated names canonicalized, tail calls marked, C1\n  2350\t   finalized. Its value is `{:js/out [...] :js/uncaught nil-or-snapshot}`.\n  2351\t\n  2352\t   `:prelude` selects how the runtime profile arrives: `:bundled` (the\n  2353\t   default) carries the prelude tree ahead of the body; `:linked` requires\n  2354\t   the modules `yang.call` and `js` from the task's link pair, then allocates\n  2355\t   the task's runtime state with `(js/init!)`.\"\n  2356\t  ([packet] (lower-packet packet {}))\n  2357\t  ([packet {:keys [prelude], :or {prelude :bundled}}]\n  2358\t   (let [main (names/canonicalize (app* 'js/run-main (lower-unit* packet)))]\n  2359\t     (u/annotate-call-sites (with-runtime prelude main)))))\n  2360\t\n  2361\t\n  2362\t(def program-medium\n  2363\t  \"The program medium's logical identity when the composition names none.\"\n  2364\t  :yang.ts/program)\n  2365\t\n  2366\t\n  2367\t(def ^:private stage-config\n  2368\t  {:diagnostic-ns diagnostic-ns,\n  2369\t   :program-medium program-medium,\n  2370\t   :ok? #(= :yang.cst/ok (:yang.cst/outcome %)),\n  2371\t   :lower (fn [state packet]\n  2372\t            (lower-packet packet {:prelude (get state :prelude :bundled)})),\n  2373\t   :option-keys [:prelude :dialect]})\n  2374\t\n  2375\t\n  2376\t(defn lower-transform\n  2377\t  \"The lowering stage's transform (`yang.core.stage/lower-transform`).\"\n  2378\t  [state packet]\n  2379\t  (core-stage/lower-transform stage-config state packet))\n  2380\t\n  2381\t\n  2382\t(defn open-stage\n  2383\t  \"A lowering stage reading CST packets from `cst-stream`, writing program\n  2384\t   batches to `program-stream`, whose logical identity is `medium`, and\n  2385\t   diagnostics to `diagnostics-stream`. The fourth argument may instead be\n  2386\t   an options map `{:medium :prelude :dialect}`.\"\n  2387\t  ([cst-stream program-stream diagnostics-stream]\n  2388\t   (core-stage/open-stage stage-config\n  2389\t                          cst-stream\n  2390\t                          program-stream\n  2391\t                          diagnostics-stream))\n  2392\t  ([cst-stream program-stream diagnostics-stream medium-or-opts]\n  2393\t   (core-stage/open-stage stage-config\n  2394\t                          cst-stream\n  2395\t                          program-stream\n  2396\t                          diagnostics-stream\n  2397\t                          medium-or-opts)))\n  2398\t\n  2399\t\n  2400\t(defn step-stage\n  2401\t  [s]\n  2402\t  (core-stage/step-stage stage-config s))\n     1\t(ns yang.typescript.antlr.safepoint\n     2\t  \"The `jssp` safepoint hook prelude (docs/design/yang.typescript.md\n     3\t   section 13; T1 plan section 8): `js.sp/loop` and `js.sp/call` for the\n     4\t   bundled profile and the linked `jssp` module. Universal AST, like the\n     5\t   base prelude; the `yang.safepoint` stage only places `(js.sp/loop)` and\n     6\t   `(js.sp/call)` at the `:loop` and `:call` sites the lowering marks, and\n     7\t   what they mean is written here.\n     8\t\n     9\t   Signals. The composition hands the task a signal stream, a sealed\n    10\t   reference in the store under `signals-key`; a host adapter appends one\n    11\t   plain value per delivered signal. Each hook reads it with `stream/poll!`,\n    12\t   which answers `:dao.stream/blocked` rather than parking, so a program\n    13\t   with no signal pending never waits at a safepoint. On a signal (or a\n    14\t   gap: values were lost, so at least one arrived) the hook delivers an\n    15\t   interrupt: it unwinds the handler stack to its outermost frame, the one\n    16\t   `js/run-main` installs, running every `finally` thunk on the way, and\n    17\t   throws the guest value `js.sp/interrupt` builds (an Error object named\n    18\t   `Interrupt`) through `js/throw` from there. No guest `catch` frame is\n    19\t   left to see it, so a `try`/`catch` around the loop does not catch it;\n    20\t   the run ends with it uncaught. Delivery is not journalled.\n    21\t\n    22\t   There is no depth accounting in T1: JavaScript has no RecursionError by\n    23\t   default (section 13), so `js.sp/call` is a poll only, and there is no\n    24\t   `:return` hook.\n    25\t\n    26\t   Two profiles, one source. `uast` is the bundled hook prelude: it loads\n    27\t   before the base prelude and may not touch a base definition while\n    28\t   loading, so it allocates only the signal cursor, and the hooks name base\n    29\t   keys only inside their bodies. `module-uast` is the same definition list\n    30\t   as the linker module `jssp`, which requires `js`, inverting the bundled\n    31\t   load order: its install child defines lambdas only, for a cursor is\n    32\t   runtime state a lift refuses, and a module closure cannot read the\n    33\t   task's ambient signal stream; the linked wrapper passes the stream's\n    34\t   reference to `(jssp/attach! signals)`, which mints the cursor. The hooks\n    35\t   reach the base prelude through its exports (`js/unwind-to`, `js/throw`,\n    36\t   `js/global-get`, ...), for `js.rt/*` is an internal store key invisible\n    37\t   across a module boundary. Every key this prelude defines is in `js.sp`.\"\n    38\t  (:require\n    39\t    [yang.core.prelude :as core]\n    40\t    [yang.core.uast :as u]\n    41\t    [yang.typescript.antlr.prelude :as prelude]))\n    42\t\n    43\t\n    44\t(def profile\n    45\t  \"The `yang.safepoint` profile this prelude implements under the bundled\n    46\t   prelude: site kind -> hook.\"\n    47\t  {:loop 'js.sp/loop, :call 'js.sp/call})\n    48\t\n    49\t\n    50\t(def linked-profile\n    51\t  \"The `yang.safepoint` profile under the linked prelude: the hooks are the\n    52\t   `jssp` module's exports, so `A'` applies `jssp/loop` and its sibling and\n    53\t   a run without the module fails closed on the unresolved hook name.\"\n    54\t  {:loop 'jssp/loop, :call 'jssp/call})\n    55\t\n    56\t\n    57\t(def signals-key\n    58\t  \"The store key the composition binds the signal stream's reference to.\"\n    59\t  'js.sp/signals)\n    60\t\n    61\t\n    62\t(def module-name\n    63\t  \"The linker module the hook prelude is published as.\"\n    64\t  'jssp)\n    65\t\n    66\t\n    67\t(def host-names\n    68\t  \"Module exports this prelude calls: the stream module's `cursor` and\n    69\t   `poll!`.\"\n    70\t  '#{stream/cursor stream/poll!})\n    71\t\n    72\t\n    73\t(def function-definitions\n    74\t  \"The single definition list, `[store-key form]` in definition order: every\n    75\t   hook function, then `attach!`. Defining them runs nothing. Both emitters\n    76\t   read it; the tests assert the module's shape against it.\"\n    77\t  '[[js.sp/interrupt\n    78\t     ;; the value an interrupt throws: an Error named Interrupt, built from\n    79\t     ;; the exported intrinsics (the error prototype is `Error.prototype`)\n    80\t     (fn []\n    81\t       (let [e (js/make-error\n    82\t                 (js/get-prop (js/global-get {:js/str \"Error\"})\n    83\t                              {:js/str \"prototype\"})\n    84\t                 {:js/str \"interrupted\"})]\n    85\t         (do (js/define-own! e\n    86\t                             {:js/str \"name\"}\n    87\t                             (js/slot {:js/str \"Interrupt\"} true false true))\n    88\t             e)))]\n    89\t    [js.sp/deliver\n    90\t     ;; down to the outermost handler frame (the run's own), then throw:\n    91\t     ;; the guest handlers above it never see the interrupt\n    92\t     (fn [sig] (do (js/unwind-to 1) (js/throw (js.sp/interrupt))))]\n    93\t    [js.sp/poll\n    94\t     (fn []\n    95\t       (let [s (stream/poll! js.sp/cursor)]\n    96\t         (if (= s :dao.stream/blocked)\n    97\t           :js/undefined\n    98\t           (if (nil? s) :js/undefined (js.sp/deliver s)))))]\n    99\t    [js.sp/loop (fn [] (js.sp/poll))]\n   100\t    [js.sp/call (fn [] (js.sp/poll))]\n   101\t    [js.sp/attach!\n   102\t     ;; the linked wrapper's call: a module closure cannot read the task's\n   103\t     ;; ambient signal stream, so the wrapper passes its reference, and the\n   104\t     ;; cursor it mints is runtime state, never install-time state.\n   105\t     ;; Idempotent, like `js/init!`\n   106\t     (fn [signals]\n   107\t       (if (= js.sp/cursor :js/uninit)\n   108\t         (do (yin/def (quote js.sp/cursor) (stream/cursor signals))\n   109\t             :js/undefined)\n   110\t         :js/undefined))]])\n   111\t\n   112\t\n   113\t(def ^:private state-definitions\n   114\t  \"The bundled profile's runtime state, allocated while loading: the signal\n   115\t   cursor, nothing else.\"\n   116\t  '[[js.sp/cursor (stream/cursor js.sp/signals)]])\n   117\t\n   118\t\n   119\t(defn- definitions->uast\n   120\t  [defs]\n   121\t  (u/seq-nodes (map (fn [[k form]] (u/def! k (u/sexp->uast form))) defs)))\n   122\t\n   123\t\n   124\t(def uast\n   125\t  \"The bundled hook prelude: functions, then the signal cursor.\"\n   126\t  (u/mark-tails (u/then (definitions->uast function-definitions)\n   127\t                        (definitions->uast state-definitions))))\n   128\t\n   129\t\n   130\t(def noop-uast\n   131\t  \"Hooks that do nothing: the derived program under them is the naive one.\"\n   132\t  (u/mark-tails (definitions->uast '[[js.sp/loop (fn [] :js/undefined)]\n   133\t                                     [js.sp/call (fn [] :js/undefined)]])))\n   134\t\n   135\t\n   136\t(defn program\n   137\t  \"The bundled derived run's tree: `hooks` (a hook prelude), then the derived\n   138\t   program `ast`.\"\n   139\t  [hooks ast]\n   140\t  (u/then hooks ast))\n   141\t\n   142\t\n   143\t(defn linked-program\n   144\t  \"The linked safepointed run's tree: `js` required and initialized, `jssp`\n   145\t   required, the signal stream the composition bound under `signals-key`\n   146\t   attached, then the derived linked program `a'`, whose own require and\n   147\t   init are idempotent re-entries. The load order is the linked one, the\n   148\t   inverse of the bundled hook-prelude-first order.\"\n   149\t  [a']\n   150\t  (u/mark-tails\n   151\t    (u/seq-nodes\n   152\t      [(u/sexp->uast (list 'require (list 'quote prelude/module-name)))\n   153\t       (u/sexp->uast (list 'require (list 'quote module-name)))\n   154\t       (u/sexp->uast '(js/init!))\n   155\t       (u/app (u/v (symbol (name module-name) \"attach!\")) (u/v signals-key))\n   156\t       a'])))\n   157\t\n   158\t\n   159\t;; =============================================================================\n   160\t;; The module emitter: the same definition list as the linker module `jssp`\n   161\t;; =============================================================================\n   162\t\n   163\t(def runtime-keys\n   164\t  \"Every key `jssp/attach!` defines, sorted: the signal cursor. It is held\n   165\t   at install time by a `:js/uninit` placeholder so the linker's scanners\n   166\t   discharge the bodies that read it.\"\n   167\t  '[js.sp/cursor])\n   168\t\n   169\t\n   170\t(defn strip\n   171\t  \"`sym` without the module's own namespace `js.sp`; any other value as it\n   172\t   is. `js/*` stays qualified: those are the base prelude's exports,\n   173\t   resolved through the registry once `js` is linked, and stripping them\n   174\t   would collide with this module's own bare keys.\"\n   175\t  [sym]\n   176\t  (core/strip \"js.sp\" sym))\n   177\t\n   178\t\n   179\t(def ^:private module-definitions\n   180\t  \"The module's definition list: a `:js/uninit` placeholder for every\n   181\t   runtime key, so each read of one is discharged by an unconditional\n   182\t   module-level definition, then every definition, stripped.\"\n   183\t  (core/module-definitions \"js.sp\" :js/uninit runtime-keys function-definitions))\n   184\t\n   185\t\n   186\t(def module-uast\n   187\t  \"The module tree: one application whose operands define hooks, then\n   188\t   deliver the pinned base prelude, applied to a lambda returning nil.\n   189\t   Every definition precedes every call, including require, so the linker's\n   190\t   scanners discharge sibling and runtime-key reads. Defining runs nothing;\n   191\t   delivery never initializes either runtime. C1 finalized, like every\n   192\t   published production tree: its `:yang/call-site` markers publish beside\n   193\t   its manifest (see `yin.vm.linker.publish`), never inside it, so the\n   194\t   manifest keeps schema 1 and its address does not move.\"\n   195\t  (u/annotate-call-sites\n   196\t    (core/module-tree module-definitions\n   197\t                      [(u/sexp->uast '(require (quote js)))])))\n   198\t\n   199\t\n   200\t(def module-exports\n   201\t  \"The module's exports: every `js.sp/` key of the definition list,\n   202\t   stripped. The cursor is internal.\"\n   203\t  (core/exports \"js.sp\" function-definitions))\n   204\t\n   205\t\n   206\t(def ^:private module-free-names\n   207\t  \"The names the module tree reads and does not define, sorted: the\n   208\t   primitives, the host exports and the base prelude's `js/*` exports its\n   209\t   manifest declares.\"\n   210\t  (core/free-name-vec module-uast))\n   211\t\n   212\t\n   213\t(defn module-spec\n   214\t  \"`yin.vm.linker.publish/publish-module!`'s spec for the module `jssp` over\n   215\t   the host registry `registry`, requiring the base prelude `js` at manifest\n   216\t   address `js-address`. A free name of the module tree is declared one of\n   217\t   three ways: a name qualified by `js` is covered by the requirement,\n   218\t   discharged by a linked `js` of equal manifest address; a bare name is a\n   219\t   primitive declared by its `vm/primitives` profile; a `ns/name` is a host\n   220\t   export declared by the profile address the registry's host module `ns`\n   221\t   publishes. A free name none of these supplies is refused before anything\n   222\t   is published. This namespace emits; it never publishes.\"\n   223\t  [registry js-address]\n   224\t  (core/module-spec {:module-name module-name,\n   225\t                     :ast module-uast,\n   226\t                     :exports module-exports,\n   227\t                     :requires {prelude/module-name js-address},\n   228\t                     :free-names module-free-names,\n   229\t                     ;; the requirement declares names qualified by `js`\n   230\t                     :skip? (fn [n] (= (name prelude/module-name) (namespace n))),\n   231\t                     :registry registry,\n   232\t                     :message \"the jssp module reads an undeclared name\",\n   233\t                     :refusal-ns \"yang.typescript.antlr\"}))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc | sed -n '1,182p;1340,1458p'\nnl -ba src/cljc/yang/core/stage.cljc | sed -n '1,130p'\nrg -n 'injected-origin|call-site|derived-envelope|defn.*transform' src/cljc/yang/safepoint.cljc\nrg -n 'safepoint/(open-stage|transform|derive|rewrite)|hooks/(program|linked-program)' src test/yang/typescript test/yang/typescript_callsite_test.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc | sed -n '1,182p;1340,1458p'\nnl -ba src/cljc/yang/core/stage.cljc | sed -n '1,130p'\nrg -n 'injected-origin|call-site|derived-envelope|defn.*transform' src/cljc/yang/safepoint.cljc\nrg -n 'safepoint/(open-stage|transform|derive|rewrite)|hooks/(program|linked-program)' src test/yang/typescript test/yang/typescript_callsite_test.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t(ns yang.clojure-callsite-test\n     2\t  \"Contract C1 for production yang.clojure (Addendum A, design §2): the\n     3\t   `:yang/call-site 1` frontend-metadata annotation of every final\n     4\t   `:application` occurrence, and the complete-coverage validation a\n     5\t   consumer runs against canonical rows.\"\n     6\t  (:require [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n     7\t            [clojure.string :as str]\n     8\t            [clojure.walk :as walk]\n     9\t            [dao.jing :as jing]\n    10\t            [dao.jing.cbor :as cbor]\n    11\t            [dao.jing.mem :as mem]\n    12\t            [dao.space.index :as space.index]\n    13\t            [dao.space.query :as query]\n    14\t            #?@(:clj [[dao.stream :as stream]\n    15\t                       [dao.stream.ringbuffer :as ring]])\n    16\t            [yang.clojure :as yang]\n    17\t            [yang.clojure.prelude :as clj-prelude]\n    18\t            [yang.core.call :as call]\n    19\t            [yang.frontend :as frontend]\n    20\t            [yang.safepoint :as safepoint]\n    21\t            [yang.tails :as tails]\n    22\t            [yin.repl :as repl]\n    23\t            [yin.repl.frontends :as repl-frontends]\n    24\t            [yin.repl.store]\n    25\t            [yin.shell.query :as shell-query]\n    26\t            [yin.vm :as vm]\n    27\t            [yin.vm.data :as data]\n    28\t            [yin.vm.encoder :as encoder]\n    29\t            [yin.vm.linker.closure :as closure]\n    30\t            [dao.stream.apply :as apply2]\n    31\t            [yin.repl.query :as repl-query]\n    32\t            [yin.vm.linker.dht :as linker-dht]\n    33\t            #?(:clj [yin.vm.linker.interpreter :as link])\n    34\t            [yin.vm.linker.publish :as publish]\n    35\t            [yin.vm.macro :as macro]\n    36\t            [yin.vm.module :as module]))\n    37\t\n    38\t\n    39\t(def ^:private origin [:source :program \"batch-1\" 0])\n    40\t\n    41\t\n    42\t(defn- project\n    43\t  [ast]\n    44\t  (let [projected (encoder/project\n    45\t                    (encoder/source-envelope :program \"batch-1\" [ast]))]\n    46\t    {:tree (first (:yin/batch projected))\n    47\t     :metadata (:yin/frontend-metadata projected)}))\n    48\t\n    49\t\n    50\t(defn- eligible-under\n    51\t  \"The eligible set of canonical `tree` under `origin`, derived here\n    52\t   directly from canonical rows and the occurrence relation,\n    53\t   independently of the producer's own helpers.\"\n    54\t  [tree origin]\n    55\t  (into #{}\n    56\t        (comp (filter (fn [[_ _ id]]\n    57\t                        (= :application (nth (get (:rows tree) id) 1))))\n    58\t              (map (fn [[_ path _]] [origin (:root tree) path])))\n    59\t        (vm/occurrences tree)))\n    60\t\n    61\t\n    62\t(defn- eligible\n    63\t  [tree]\n    64\t  (eligible-under tree origin))\n    65\t\n    66\t\n    67\t(defn- occurrence-pairs\n    68\t  \"The `[root-address path]` of every `:application` occurrence of\n    69\t   canonical `tree` — the projection a consumer derives from canonical\n    70\t   rows alone, origin-free (design §2.2: the origin values of a\n    71\t   per-occurrence table are the producer's correspondence claim).\"\n    72\t  [tree]\n    73\t  (into #{}\n    74\t        (comp (filter (fn [[_ _ id]]\n    75\t                        (= :application (nth (get (:rows tree) id) 1))))\n    76\t              (map (fn [[_ path _]] [(:root tree) path])))\n    77\t        (vm/occurrences tree)))\n    78\t\n    79\t\n    80\t(defn- marked-pairs\n    81\t  \"The `[root-address path]` projection of a C1 marker relation.\"\n    82\t  [metadata]\n    83\t  (into #{}\n    84\t        (comp (filter #(= :yang/call-site (nth % 3)))\n    85\t              (map (fn [[_ r path _ _]] [r path])))\n    86\t        metadata))\n    87\t\n    88\t\n    89\t(defn- row-origins\n    90\t  \"The distinct occurrence origins a C1 marker relation carries.\"\n    91\t  [metadata]\n    92\t  (into #{} (map first) (filter #(= :yang/call-site (nth % 3)) metadata)))\n    93\t\n    94\t\n    95\t(defn- expansion-origin?\n    96\t  [o]\n    97\t  (and (vector? o) (= :expansion (first o))))\n    98\t\n    99\t\n   100\t(defn- marked\n   101\t  [metadata]\n   102\t  (into #{}\n   103\t        (comp (filter #(= :yang/call-site (nth % 3)))\n   104\t              (map (fn [[o r path _ _]] [o r path])))\n   105\t        metadata))\n   106\t\n   107\t\n   108\t(defn- failure-rule\n   109\t  [f]\n   110\t  (try (f) ::no-failure\n   111\t       (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Exception :cljs :default) e\n   112\t         (:rule (ex-data e)))))\n   113\t\n   114\t\n   115\t(deftest equality-gate-test\n   116\t  (testing \"native compile: eligible set equals marker set\"\n   117\t    (let [ast (yang/compile '(+ (* 2 3) 4))\n   118\t          {:keys [tree metadata]} (project ast)]\n   119\t      (is (= #{[origin (:root tree) []]\n   120\t               [origin (:root tree) [[3 0]]]}\n   121\t             (marked metadata)))\n   122\t      (is (= (eligible tree) (marked metadata)))\n   123\t      (is (true? (yang/validate-call-site-coverage! tree metadata origin)))\n   124\t      (is (true? (yang/validate-ast-call-sites! ast origin)))\n   125\t      (is (every? (fn [[o r _ k v]]\n   126\t                    (and (= origin o) (= (:root tree) r)\n   127\t                         (= :yang/call-site k) (= 1 v)))\n   128\t                  (filter #(= :yang/call-site (nth % 3)) metadata)))))\n   129\t  (testing \"compile-program, native and argument-vector/outcome paths\"\n   130\t    (doseq [ast [(yang/compile-program\n   131\t                   '[(defn f\n   132\t                       [x]\n   133\t                       (+ x 1)) (defn g\n   134\t                                  [x]\n   135\t                                  (f (* x 2))) (g 21)])\n   136\t                 (yang/compile-program\n   137\t                   '[(defn f\n   138\t                       [x]\n   139\t                       (+ x 1)) (f 2)] true yang/unit-opts)]]\n   140\t      (let [{:keys [tree metadata]} (project ast)]\n   141\t        (is (= (eligible tree) (marked metadata)))\n   142\t        (is (true? (yang/validate-call-site-coverage! tree metadata origin))))))\n   143\t  (testing \"lower-unit: the linked production path, library included\"\n   144\t    (let [ast (yang/lower-unit '[(defn f\n   145\t                                   [x]\n   146\t                                   (+ x 1)) (f 2)])\n   147\t          {:keys [tree metadata]} (project ast)]\n   148\t      (is (< 10 (count (marked metadata))))\n   149\t      (is (= (eligible tree) (marked metadata)))\n   150\t      (is (true? (yang/validate-call-site-coverage! tree metadata origin)))))\n   151\t  (testing \"the clj prelude module tree is finalized\"\n   152\t    (let [ast yang.clojure.prelude/module-uast\n   153\t          {:keys [tree metadata]} (project ast)]\n   154\t      (is (= (eligible tree) (marked metadata)))\n   155\t      (is (true? (yang/validate-call-site-coverage! tree metadata origin))))))\n   156\t\n   157\t\n   158\t(deftest boundary-test\n   159\t  (testing \"yin/def gets an occurrence annotation\"\n   160\t    (let [ast (yang/compile '(def x (fn [a] (+ a 1))))]\n   161\t      (is (= 1 (:yang/call-site ast)))\n   162\t      (is (= 1 (get-in ast [:operands 1 :body :yang/call-site])))\n   163\t      (is (true? (yang/validate-ast-call-sites! ast origin)))))\n   164\t  (testing \"a dedicated stream operation is not an application site\"\n   165\t    (let [ast (yang/compile '(dao.stream.apply/call :op/echo (+ 1 2)))\n   166\t          {:keys [tree metadata]} (project ast)]\n   167\t      (is (= :dao.stream.apply/call (:type ast)))\n   168\t      (is (not (contains? ast :yang/call-site)))\n   169\t      ;; its operand application is an ordinary occurrence and is marked\n   170\t      (is (= #{[origin (:root tree) [[3 0]]]} (marked metadata)))\n   171\t      (is (true? (yang/validate-call-site-coverage! tree metadata origin)))))\n   172\t  (testing \"stream and continuation nodes are never marked\"\n   173\t    (let [ast (yang/annotate-call-sites\n   174\t                {:type :application\n   175\t                 :operator {:type :variable :name 'f}\n   176\t                 :operands [{:type :stream/make :buffer 1}\n   177\t                            {:type :vm/current-continuation}]})]\n   178\t      (is (= 1 (:yang/call-site ast)))\n   179\t      (is (not (contains? (first (:operands ast)) :yang/call-site)))\n   180\t      (is (not (contains? (second (:operands ast)) :yang/call-site))))))\n   181\t\n   182\t\n  1340\t\n  1341\t(def ^:private sp-ast\n  1342\t  \"`((fn [w] (w w)) (fn [w] (f w)))`, both lambdas site-marked (`:call`,\n  1343\t   `:loop`) and every application C1-marked, tails marked as a frontend\n  1344\t   would.\"\n  1345\t  (yang/annotate-call-sites\n  1346\t    (tails/mark-tails\n  1347\t      (sp-app (vary-meta (sp-lam '[w] (sp-app (sp-var 'w) (sp-var 'w)))\n  1348\t                         assoc :yang/site :call)\n  1349\t              (vary-meta (sp-lam '[w] (sp-app (sp-var 'f) (sp-var 'w)))\n  1350\t                         assoc :yang/site :loop)))))\n  1351\t\n  1352\t\n  1353\t(def ^:private sp-profile {:loop 'h/loop :call 'h/call})\n  1354\t(def ^:private sp-origin (vm/source-origin :m [:t 0] 0))\n  1355\t(def ^:private sp-injected-origin [:source :test/publication \"safepoint-c1\" 0])\n  1356\t\n  1357\t\n  1358\t(defn- sp-projected\n  1359\t  [ast]\n  1360\t  (encoder/project (encoder/source-envelope :m [:t 0] [ast])))\n  1361\t\n  1362\t\n  1363\t(defn- entry-set\n  1364\t  [correspondence kind]\n  1365\t  (into #{} (filter #(= kind (:kind %))) (:entries correspondence)))\n  1366\t\n  1367\t\n  1368\t(deftest safepoint-c1-preservation-test\n  1369\t  (let [input (sp-projected sp-ast)\n  1370\t        input-tree (first (:yin/batch input))\n  1371\t        input-rows (filterv #(= :yang/call-site (nth % 3))\n  1372\t                            (:yin/frontend-metadata input))]\n  1373\t    (is (seq input-rows) \"the input envelope carries a C1 claim\")\n  1374\t    (testing \"without a supplied injected origin, surviving occurrences\n  1375\t              keep their own origin at their shifted paths and injected\n  1376\t              occurrences are identified but unclaimed\"\n  1377\t      (let [{:keys [envelope correspondence]}\n  1378\t            (safepoint/derive-envelope input sp-profile :m')\n  1379\t            derived-tree (first (:yin/batch envelope))\n  1380\t            md (:yin/frontend-metadata envelope)\n  1381\t            surviving (entry-set correspondence :surviving)\n  1382\t            injected (entry-set correspondence :safepoint/injected)]\n  1383\t        (is (some? correspondence))\n  1384\t        (is (= (count input-rows) (count surviving))\n  1385\t            \"every claimed input occurrence survives (wrapping never drops one)\")\n  1386\t        (is (= (into #{} (map :input) surviving)\n  1387\t               (into #{} (map #(vec (take 3 %))) input-rows))\n  1388\t            \"the correspondence names every claimed input occurrence\")\n  1389\t        (is (= (into #{} (map :output) surviving) (marked md))\n  1390\t            \"the derived rows are exactly the surviving occurrences\")\n  1391\t        (is (= #{sp-origin} (row-origins md))\n  1392\t            \"surviving rows keep the input rows' own origin, none fabricated\")\n  1393\t        (is (seq injected) \"the hook insertions are recorded as injected\")\n  1394\t        (is (every? #(not (contains? % :origin)) injected)\n  1395\t            \"with no origin supplied by the caller, none is invented\")\n  1396\t        (is (= (into #{} (map (fn [e] [(:root derived-tree) (:path e)])) injected)\n  1397\t               (into #{} (remove (into #{}\n  1398\t                                       (map (fn [[_ r p]] [r p])\n  1399\t                                            (map :output surviving)))\n  1400\t                                 (occurrence-pairs derived-tree))))\n  1401\t            \"the unclaimed derived occurrences are exactly the injected ones\")\n  1402\t        (testing \"canonical invariance: C1 carriage changes no row or root\"\n  1403\t          (let [plain (safepoint/derive-envelope\n  1404\t                        (sp-projected (strip-call-sites sp-ast))\n  1405\t                        sp-profile :m')]\n  1406\t            (is (= (:root derived-tree)\n  1407\t                   (:root (first (:yin/batch (:envelope plain))))))\n  1408\t            (is (= derived-tree (first (:yin/batch (:envelope plain)))))))))\n  1409\t    (testing \"with a caller-supplied admission origin, the derived table\n  1410\t              covers the derived tree completely and the injected rows\n  1411\t              carry that origin alone\"\n  1412\t      (let [{:keys [envelope correspondence]}\n  1413\t            (safepoint/derive-envelope input sp-profile :m'\n  1414\t                                       {:injected-origin sp-injected-origin})\n  1415\t            derived-tree (first (:yin/batch envelope))\n  1416\t            md (:yin/frontend-metadata envelope)\n  1417\t            surviving (entry-set correspondence :surviving)\n  1418\t            injected (entry-set correspondence :safepoint/injected)]\n  1419\t        (is (= (occurrence-pairs derived-tree) (marked-pairs md))\n  1420\t            \"the recomputed table covers every derived application\")\n  1421\t        (is (true? (yang/validate-call-site-coverage!\n  1422\t                     derived-tree md sp-injected-origin\n  1423\t                     {:declared? true :per-occurrence-origins? true})))\n  1424\t        (is (every? #(= sp-injected-origin (:origin %)) injected))\n  1425\t        (is (= (into #{} (map (fn [e] [(:origin e) (:root derived-tree) (:path e)]))\n  1426\t                     injected)\n  1427\t               (into #{} (filter #(= sp-injected-origin (first %))) (marked md)))\n  1428\t            \"the injected rows are exactly the injected correspondence entries\")\n  1429\t        (is (= (into #{} (map :output) surviving)\n  1430\t               (into #{} (filter #(= sp-origin (first %))) (marked md)))\n  1431\t            \"the surviving rows keep the input origin\")))\n  1432\t    (testing \"an ambiguous or stale input row is refused attribution,\n  1433\t              never guessed\"\n  1434\t      (let [victim (first input-rows)\n  1435\t            other-origin [:source :other-publisher \"batch-9\" 0]\n  1436\t            bad (assoc input :yin/frontend-metadata\n  1437\t                       (into (:yin/frontend-metadata input)\n  1438\t                             [[other-origin (nth victim 1) (nth victim 2)\n  1439\t                               :yang/call-site 1]\n  1440\t                              [sp-origin (:root input-tree) [99]\n  1441\t                               :yang/call-site 1]]))\n  1442\t            {:keys [envelope correspondence]}\n  1443\t            (safepoint/derive-envelope bad sp-profile :m'\n  1444\t                                       {:injected-origin sp-injected-origin})\n  1445\t            unmapped (entry-set correspondence :unmapped)]\n  1446\t        (is (= #{(vec (take 3 victim))\n  1447\t                 [other-origin (nth victim 1) (nth victim 2)]\n  1448\t                 [sp-origin (:root input-tree) [99]]}\n  1449\t               (into #{} (map :input) unmapped))\n  1450\t            \"both claims on the double-claimed occurrence and the stale\n  1451\t             occurrence are unmapped\")\n  1452\t        (is (not (contains? (marked (:yin/frontend-metadata envelope))\n  1453\t                            (some #(when (= (vec (take 3 victim)) (:input %))\n  1454\t                                     (:output %))\n  1455\t                                  (entry-set correspondence :surviving))))\n  1456\t            \"no surviving row is emitted for the refused occurrence\")))))\n  1457\t\n  1458\t\n     1\t(ns yang.core.stage\n     2\t  \"The lowering stage every language shares (docs/design/yang.typescript.md\n     3\t   §17, lift L2): CST packets in, program batches on port `:program`,\n     4\t   diagnostics on port `:diagnostics`. A language supplies a `config`:\n     5\t\n     6\t     :diagnostic-ns   string, the namespace of its diagnostic keys\n     7\t     :program-medium  the program medium's default logical identity\n     8\t     :ok?             (fn [packet]) true when the packet is lowered\n     9\t     :lower           (fn [state packet]) the program tree of an ok packet\n    10\t     :option-keys     the state keys an options map may carry besides\n    11\t                      `:medium`\"\n    12\t  (:require\n    13\t    [yang.stage :as stage]\n    14\t    [yin.vm.encoder :as encoder]))\n    15\t\n    16\t\n    17\t(defn diagnostic\n    18\t  \"The record of a lowering diagnostic `data` for `unit`.\"\n    19\t  [diagnostic-ns unit data message]\n    20\t  (merge {:yang.cst/unit unit, :message message}\n    21\t         (select-keys data [(keyword diagnostic-ns \"diagnostic\") :rule\n    22\t                            :construct :span :name])))\n    23\t\n    24\t\n    25\t(defn lower-transform\n    26\t  \"The lowering stage's transform: an ok packet becomes one program batch on\n    27\t   port `:program`, a source envelope (`yin.vm.encoder/source-envelope`)\n    28\t   whose one member is the map AST `(:lower config)` returns, so its\n    29\t   `:yang/site` marks reach the frontend-metadata side table when the\n    30\t   encoder projects it. The medium is the state's `:medium` and the batch\n    31\t   token is the packet's unit. A packet that is not ok, or a lowering\n    32\t   diagnostic, becomes one record on port `:diagnostics` and no program.\n    33\t   Stateless.\"\n    34\t  [{:keys [diagnostic-ns program-medium ok? lower]} state packet]\n    35\t  (let [unit (:yang.cst/unit packet)\n    36\t        diagnostic-key (keyword diagnostic-ns \"diagnostic\")]\n    37\t    (if (ok? packet)\n    38\t      (try\n    39\t        [state [[:program (encoder/source-envelope\n    40\t                            (get state :medium program-medium)\n    41\t                            unit\n    42\t                            [(lower state packet)])]]]\n    43\t        ;; ClojureDart's ex-info type is not catchable by name portably;\n    44\t        ;; anything without a diagnostic in its ex-data is rethrown below\n    45\t        (catch #?(:cljd Object\n    46\t                  :clj clojure.lang.ExceptionInfo\n    47\t                  :cljs ExceptionInfo)\n    48\t               e\n    49\t          (if (get (ex-data e) diagnostic-key)\n    50\t            [state\n    51\t             [[:diagnostics\n    52\t               (diagnostic diagnostic-ns unit (ex-data e) (ex-message e))]]]\n    53\t            (throw e))))\n    54\t      [state\n    55\t       [[:diagnostics {:yang.cst/unit unit,\n    56\t                       diagnostic-key (keyword diagnostic-ns\n    57\t                                               (name (:yang.cst/outcome\n    58\t                                                       packet))),\n    59\t                       :errors (:yang.cst/errors packet)}]]])))\n    60\t\n    61\t\n    62\t(defn open-stage\n    63\t  \"A lowering stage reading CST packets from `cst-stream`, writing program\n    64\t   batches to `program-stream`, whose logical identity is `medium`, and\n    65\t   diagnostics to `diagnostics-stream`. The fourth argument may instead be\n    66\t   an options map of `:medium` and the config's `:option-keys`; the fifth,\n    67\t   `max-digits`, is the digit budget of every packet that declares none.\"\n    68\t  ([config cst-stream program-stream diagnostics-stream]\n    69\t   (open-stage config\n    70\t               cst-stream\n    71\t               program-stream\n    72\t               diagnostics-stream\n    73\t               (:program-medium config)))\n    74\t  ([{:keys [program-medium option-keys]}\n    75\t    cst-stream\n    76\t    program-stream\n    77\t    diagnostics-stream\n    78\t    medium-or-opts]\n    79\t   (stage/open cst-stream\n    80\t               {:program program-stream, :diagnostics diagnostics-stream}\n    81\t               (if (map? medium-or-opts)\n    82\t                 (let [{:keys [medium], :or {medium program-medium}}\n    83\t                       medium-or-opts]\n    84\t                   (assoc (select-keys medium-or-opts option-keys)\n    85\t                          :medium medium))\n    86\t                 {:medium medium-or-opts})))\n    87\t  ([_config cst-stream program-stream diagnostics-stream medium max-digits]\n    88\t   (stage/open cst-stream\n    89\t               {:program program-stream, :diagnostics diagnostics-stream}\n    90\t               {:medium medium, :max-digits max-digits})))\n    91\t\n    92\t\n    93\t(defn step-stage\n    94\t  [config s]\n    95\t  (stage/step s (partial lower-transform config)))\n38:     exception is the C1 claim: when the input claims `:yang/call-site`\n64:(def call-site-key\n65:  \"The frontend-metadata key of the call-site occurrence contract C1,\n67:  :yang/call-site)\n298:(defn- derive-call-sites\n303:   occurrence is claimed only under `injected-origin`, the admission\n312:  [frontend-metadata tree derived hooks injected-origin]\n316:                             (= call-site-key (nth row 3))))\n357:                                                  call-site-key (nth r 4)])\n372:                                      injected-origin\n373:                                      (assoc :origin injected-origin)))\n375:            injected-rows (when injected-origin\n377:                                   [injected-origin (:root derived) p\n378:                                    call-site-key 1])\n413:   `opts` may supply `:injected-origin`, the caller's admission origin\n418:  ([envelope profile medium {:keys [injected-origin]}]\n419:   (when (and injected-origin (not (vm/occurrence-origin? injected-origin)))\n420:     (throw (ex-info \"Malformed injected call-site origin\"\n421:                     {:rule :origin, :origin injected-origin})))\n430:         (derive-call-sites frontend-metadata tree derived\n432:                            injected-origin)\n450:(defn transform\ntest/yang/typescript/antlr/linked_prelude_test.cljc:259:        {:keys [envelope]} (safepoint/derive-envelope projected\ntest/yang/typescript/antlr/linked_prelude_test.cljc:303:            (on-every-vm (hooks/linked-program (derived-ast spin)) [2])))\ntest/yang/typescript/antlr/linked_prelude_test.cljc:306:            (on-every-vm (hooks/linked-program (derived-ast caught)) [2]))))\ntest/yang/typescript/antlr/linked_prelude_test.cljc:318:            (on-every-vm (hooks/linked-program (derived-ast spin-then-log))\ntest/yang/typescript/antlr/e2e_test.clj:82:      (safepoint/open-stage rows derived ledger profile :e2e/derived))\ntest/yang/typescript/antlr/e2e_test.clj:111:                       (hooks/program\ntest/yang/typescript/antlr/safepoint_test.clj:134:        {:keys [envelope record]} (safepoint/derive-envelope projected profile\ntest/yang/typescript/antlr/safepoint_test.clj:209:            (on-every-vm (hooks/program hooks/uast\ntest/yang/typescript/antlr/safepoint_test.clj:215:            (on-every-vm (hooks/program hooks/uast\ntest/yang/typescript/antlr/safepoint_test.clj:230:            (on-every-vm (hooks/program hooks/uast\ntest/yang/typescript/antlr/safepoint_test.clj:240:            (on-every-vm (hooks/program hooks/uast\ntest/yang/typescript/antlr/safepoint_test.clj:256:              (on-every-vm (hooks/program hooks/uast\ntest/yang/typescript/antlr/safepoint_test.clj:276:          noop (on-every-vm (hooks/program hooks/noop-uast\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/siteset.cljc:345:   (`yang.safepoint/derive-record`) is materialized beside it and its\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/siteset.cljc:396:                           (safepoint/derive-record\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yang/safepoint.cljc | sed -n '1,48p;290,503p'\nnl -ba test/yang/typescript/antlr/e2e_test.clj | sed -n '49,125p'\nnl -ba test/yang/typescript/antlr/linked_prelude_test.cljc | sed -n '247,278p'\nnl -ba test/yang/typescript/antlr/safepoint_test.clj | sed -n '119,150p'\nrg -n 'defn (ast-side-tables|application-occurrences|occurrences)|semantic-bytecode-grammar|frontend-metadata' src/cljc/yin/vm.cljc | head -35\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yang/safepoint.cljc | sed -n '1,48p;290,503p'\nnl -ba test/yang/typescript/antlr/e2e_test.clj | sed -n '49,125p'\nnl -ba test/yang/typescript/antlr/linked_prelude_test.cljc | sed -n '247,278p'\nnl -ba test/yang/typescript/antlr/safepoint_test.clj | sed -n '119,150p'\nrg -n 'defn (ast-side-tables|application-occurrences|occurrences)|semantic-bytecode-grammar|frontend-metadata' src/cljc/yin/vm.cljc | head -35\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t(ns yang.safepoint\n     2\t  \"The safepoint stage (Architect safepoint-interpreter design, slice 1): a\n     3\t   pure rewrite of a canonical program tree `A` into a derived tree `A'` that\n     4\t   applies a hook at every frontend-marked site the profile maps.\n     5\t   Language-neutral: it knows the Universal AST row grammar and the\n     6\t   frontend-metadata side table, nothing about any guest language. The hooks'\n     7\t   meaning lives in a per-language hook prelude; the evaluator never learns\n     8\t   what a safepoint is.\n     9\t\n    10\t   - A site is a `:lambda` occurrence the frontend marked with `:yang/site`\n    11\t     metadata, which projection puts in the side table as\n    12\t     `[origin root path :yang/site kind]`. A profile `{kind hook-symbol}`\n    13\t     selects sites; a kind it omits is not inserted.\n    14\t   - Insertion prefixes the site's body with an ordinary `:application` of\n    15\t     the hook, sequenced through a lambda whose one binder is `binder`, in a\n    16\t     reserved namespace: no new tag, no gensym counter. An exit kind\n    17\t     (`exit-kinds`: `:return` at `:call` sites) wraps the body instead: its\n    18\t     hook is applied to the body's value, so it runs on normal exit only.\n    19\t   - A mark's value is a kind, or a vector `[kind datum ...]`: the data\n    20\t     (a function's name and line, a statement's line) are literals the\n    21\t     frontend knows and the derived tree may need. A profile entry is a\n    22\t     hook symbol, or `{:hook symbol :operands true}` to apply the hook to\n    23\t     the mark's data. A statement kind (`statement-kinds`: `:line`) marks\n    24\t     any node, not a lambda; its hook is applied before the node, which\n    25\t     is sequenced after it.\n    26\t   - Every tail mark is stripped and recomputed over the whole derived tree\n    27\t     (`yang.tails`): a wrapped body's old tail calls would otherwise skip\n    28\t     its wrapper. With no site selected `A'` is `A`, row for row.\n    29\t   - `A` is never modified. Names, the ledger and publication refer to it;\n    30\t     the link is a `:derive` record with input `A`, output `A'`, function\n    31\t     `function`, and a profile pinning the hook map and the address of the\n    32\t     sorted site set. Insertion is deterministic, so a repeat writes the\n    33\t     same record.\n    34\t   - `A'` leaves on the stage's own medium in a projected envelope whose\n    35\t     batch token is the record's address, so its occurrence origin is an\n    36\t     ordinary `[:source medium' token 0]`. No side table is copied: an `A'`\n    37\t     node's facts are a join back to `A` through the site set. The one\n    38\t     exception is the C1 claim: when the input claims `:yang/call-site`\n    39\t     coverage, `derive-envelope` recomputes its rows over `A'` (never\n    40\t     copies them — paths shift) and records the input→output occurrence\n    41\t     correspondence as data.\"\n    42\t  (:require\n    43\t    [dao.jing :as jing]\n    44\t    [yang.stage :as stage]\n    45\t    [yang.tails :as tails]\n    46\t    [yin.vm :as vm]))\n    47\t\n    48\t\n   290\t                    :nodes (doseq [[i child] (map-indexed vector (or value []))]\n   291\t                             (walk2 child (conj in-path [pos i])\n   292\t                                    (conj out-path [pos i])))\n   293\t                    nil)))]\n   294\t        (walk2 ast [] []))\n   295\t      {:surviving @surviving :injected @injected}))\n   296\t\n   297\t\n   298\t(defn- derive-call-sites\n   299\t  \"Recompute the C1 rows of the derived tree from the input tree's own\n   300\t   rows: `{:metadata rows :correspondence c}`, or nil when the input\n   301\t   carries no C1 claim for `tree`. A surviving occurrence keeps its\n   302\t   input row's origin at its tracked output path. An injected\n   303\t   occurrence is claimed only under `injected-origin`, the admission\n   304\t   origin the caller supplies; without one it is recorded as injected\n   305\t   and left unclaimed. An input row whose occurrence is claimed by two\n   306\t   origins, or that names no application occurrence of the input tree,\n   307\t   is refused attribution (`:unmapped`) — never guessed. Every mapped\n   308\t   output place is verified against the derived tree's own application\n   309\t   occurrences; a place that is not an application there (the exit\n   310\t   hook's literal operands, say) is likewise `:unmapped`\n   311\t   (`:output-not-an-application`), never emitted as a row.\"\n   312\t  [frontend-metadata tree derived hooks injected-origin]\n   313\t  (let [rows (filterv (fn [row]\n   314\t                        (and (sequential? row) (= 5 (count row))\n   315\t                             (= (:root tree) (nth row 1))\n   316\t                             (= call-site-key (nth row 3))))\n   317\t                      frontend-metadata)]\n   318\t    (when (seq rows)\n   319\t      (let [{:keys [surviving injected]}\n   320\t            (track-occurrences (vm/semantic-bytecode->ast tree) hooks)\n   321\t            eligible (into #{} (map second) (vm/application-occurrences tree))\n   322\t            derived-eligible (into #{}\n   323\t                                   (map second)\n   324\t                                   (vm/application-occurrences derived))\n   325\t            by-path (