ted (into (:unmapped parts)\n   387\t                                                             refused-injected))))}}))))\n   388\t\n   389\t\n   390\t(defn derive-record\n   391\t  \"The `:derive` record linking canonical root `input` to derived root\n   392\t   `output`: function `function`, profile pinning the hook map and the\n   393\t   address of the sorted site set.\"\n   394\t  [input output profile selected]\n   395\t  {:yin.ledger/op :derive,\n   396\t   :yin.ledger/input input,\n   397\t   :yin.ledger/output output,\n   398\t   :yin.ledger/function function,\n   399\t   :yin.ledger/profile {:yang.safepoint/hooks profile,\n   400\t                        :yang.safepoint/sites (jing/segment-key\n   401\t                                                (site-set selected))}})\n   402\t\n   403\t\n   404\t(defn derive-envelope\n   405\t  \"One projected envelope from the row medium to the derived one:\n   406\t   `{:envelope e' :record r :record-address a}`. The run member of the input\n   407\t   is `A`; `e'` carries `A'` alone, on `medium`, with token `a`.\n   408\t\n   409\t   When the input envelope's frontend-metadata claims C1 for the run\n   410\t   member, `e'` carries the recomputed rows of `A'` and the answer\n   411\t   carries `:correspondence`, the explicit input→output occurrence\n   412\t   correspondence (also on `e'` as `:yang.safepoint/correspondence`).\n   413\t   `opts` may supply `:injected-origin`, the caller's admission origin\n   414\t   for the injected hook applications; without one they stay\n   415\t   unclaimed. No origin is ever derived from the trees' structure.\"\n   416\t  ([envelope profile medium]\n   417\t   (derive-envelope envelope profile medium nil))\n   418\t  ([envelope profile medium {:keys [injected-origin]}]\n   419\t   (when (and injected-origin (not (vm/occurrence-origin? injected-origin)))\n   420\t     (throw (ex-info \"Malformed injected call-site origin\"\n   421\t                     {:rule :origin, :origi