g out to any delegate CLI. It is reference\ndocs/agents/team.md:2:description: Team roster, role routing, and reviewer-independence rules for datom.world\ndocs/agents/team.md:7:Canonical guide for the shared roster, role routing, and reviewer independence.\ndocs/agents/team.md:10:delegate session protocol and CLI recipes live in\ndocs/agents/team.md:11:[`delegate-invocation-reference.md`](./delegate-invocation-reference.md).\ndocs/agents/team.md:17:delegation prompt template under `docs/agents/roles/`. Review is one role\ndocs/agents/team.md:18:backed by one file, `roles/reviewer.md`, covering adversarial, routine, and\ndocs/agents/team.md:25:| [Architect](roles/architect.md)                   | Axioms, invariants, boundaries, architecture                                                           |\ndocs/agents/team.md:33:| [Review](roles/reviewer.md)                       | Adversarial defect discovery, routine correctness/portability checks, and security capability sign-off |\ndocs/agents/team.md:100:|                             | **Best for:** Architecture definition, security sign-offs.         | one-shot implementations where strict rigor is overkill.            |\ndocs/agents/team.md:158:|                             | moderate-complexity implementation, and subagent fallback.         | specialist work with focused tests and independent review.          |\ndocs/agents/team.md:193:|                             |                                                                    | focus, not a reviewer.                                              |\ndocs/agents/team.md:242:independent defect discovery. Never silently substitute a same-family reviewer.\ndocs/agents/team.md:246:independence: the `qwen` lane's `deepseek-v4-pro` is a **DeepSeek**\ndocs/agents/team.md:251:Routine review applies only when independent; architectural or security review\ndocs/agents/team.md:258:- **The standing reviewer bench** is wider than the implementation bench:\ndocs/agents/team.md:260:  as a standing review destination. The independence rule is unchanged: the\ndocs/agents/team.md:261:  reviewer must be a different model family from the author.\ndocs/agents/team.md:273:- Never relax the independence rule or skip reviews on small slices; the fix\ndocs/agents/team.md:274:  for throughput is more reviewers, not fewer reviews.\n    55\t;; as `[origin root-address path :yang/call-site 1]`, where the first\n    56\t;; three coordinates are the site id. The key carries no callee identity,\n    57\t;; source arity, or ambient classification. It is distinct from\n    58\t;; `:yang/site`, the safepoint mark, which travels as node metadata.\n    59\t;; Dedicated node kinds (`:dao.stream.apply/call`, stream and\n    60\t;; continuation nodes) are not `:application` nodes and are never marked.\n    61\t\n    62\t(def call-site-key\n    63\t  \"The reserved frontend-metadata key of contract C1.\"\n    64\t  :yang/call-site)\n    65\t\n    66\t\n    67\t(def call-site-version\n    68\t  \"The version value a C1 marker carries.\"\n    69\t  1)\n    70\t\n    71\t\n    72\t(def ^:private ^:dynamic *call-site-finalizing*\n    73\t  \"True while an owning production entry point compiles a tree, so the\n    74\t   recursive `compile-form` calls inside it defer marking to that entry\n    75\t   point's single finalization walk over the finished tree.\"\n    76\t  false)\n    77\t\n    78\t\n    79\t(defn annotate-call-sites\n    80\t  \"The finished map AST `node` with `call-site-key`/`call-site-version`\n    81\t   on every `:application` node, at every depth the row grammar knows.\n    82\t   Literal payloads are data, never syntax, and are not walked. Marking\n    83\t   is idempotent and preserves node metadata and every other key, so\n    84\t   canonical rows, roots, and executable outcomes are unchanged.\n    85\t\n    86\t   The walk itself is `yang.core.uast/annotate-call-sites`, shared with\n    87\t   the other frontends' module trees; this frontend owns the contract's\n    88\t   constants and its validation over canonical rows.\"\n    89\t  [node]\n    90\t  (u/annotate-call-sites node))\n    91\t\n    92\t\n    93\t(defn eligible-application-sites\n    94\t  \"The eligible C1 site set of canonical `tree` (`{:root :rows}`) under\n    95\t   `origin`: one `[origin root-address path]` per `:application`\n    96\t   occurrence, derived from the occurrence relation and the row tags.\"\n    97\t  [tree origin]\n    98\t  (into #{}\n    99\t        (map (fn [[root path]] [origin root path]))\n   100\t        (vm/application-occurrences tree)))\n   101\t\n   102\t\n   103\t(defn call-site-metadata\n   104\t  \"The C1 frontend-metadata rows of canonical `tree` (`{:root :rows}`)\n   105\t   under `origin`: one `[origin root-address path :yang/call-site 1]`\n   106\t   per eligible application occurrence, in canonical-byte order\n   107\t   (`jing/canonical-compare`). This is\n   108\t   the finalizer for trees that exist only as canonical rows — the\n   109\t   expander's final tree, a published module's tree — where no map AST\n   110\t   remains for `annotate-call-sites` to walk.\"\n   111\t  [tree origin]\n   112\t  (vec (sort jing/canonical-compare\n   113\t             (map (fn [[root path]]\n   114\t                    [origin root path call-site-key call-site-version])\n   115\t                  (vm/application-occurrences tree)))))\n   116\t\n   117\t\n   118\t(defn marked-application-sites\n   119\t  \"The deduped C1 marker set of a frontend-metadata relation: one\n   120\t   `[origin root-address path]` per distinct `:yang/call-site` row.\n   121\t   Duplicate identical transport deliveries dedupe to the same fact.\"\n   122\t  [frontend-metadata]\n   123\t  (into #{}\n   124\t        (comp (filter (fn [row]\n   125\t                        (and (= 5 (count row)) (= call-site-key (nth row 3)))))\n   126\t              (map (fn [[origin root path _ _]] [origin root path])))\n   127\t        (distinct frontend-metadata)))\n   128\t\n   129\t\n   130\t(defn- marker-row?\n   131\t  \"True when frontend-metadata `row` claims the C1 key: a sequential row\n   132\t   whose fourth coordinate is `call-site-key`. A claiming row of any\n   133\t   other arity is malformed, never a row to filter away silently.\"\n   134\t  [row]\n   135\t  (and (sequential? row)\n   136\t       (<= 4 (count row))\n   137\t       (= call-site-key (nth row 3))))\n   138\t\n   139\t\n   140\t(defn validate-call-site-coverage!\n   141\t  \"Validate a complete-coverage C1 claim: the marker set of\n   142\t   `frontend-metadata` for canonical `tree` under `origin` must equal\n   143\t   the eligible application set. Returns true when the claim holds.\n   144\t\n   145\t   A row that claims the C1 key but is not a five-coordinate\n   146\t   `[origin root-address path key value]` row is malformed and is\n   147\t   rejected, never silently filtered. The delivery mode is `opts`:\n   148\t\n   149\t   - default (transport): the relation arrived over a medium, where an\n   150\t     at-least-once delivery may repeat a row; duplicate identical\n   151\t     deliveries dedupe to the same fact;\n   152\t   - `{:declared? true}`: the relation is a declared canonical table —\n   153\t     the side table a producer published as the tree's table — where a\n   154\t     duplicate entry is a second, conflicting claim to one fact and is\n   155\t     rejected;\n   156\t   - `{:per-occurrence-origins? true}`: the tree's occurrences do not\n   157\t     share one origin — the expander's final tree, whose rows carry\n   158\t     each occurrence's own admission or generating-expansion origin\n   159\t     (design §2.1, §2.3). Coverage is then compared on the\n   160\t     `[root-address path]` projection — the part a consumer derives\n   161\t     from canonical rows alone — and every marker's origin is held to\n   162\t     a well-formed occurrence origin; the origin VALUES are the\n   163\t     producer's correspondence claim, not something a consumer can\n   164\t     re-derive.\n   165\t\n   166\t   Conflicting values at one site, an unsupported marker version, a\n   167\t   malformed origin, a marker naming no occurrence, a marker on a\n   168\t   non-application occurrence, and missing or extra markers each\n   169\t   throw, naming the failed `:rule`.\"\n   170\t  ([tree frontend-metadata origin]\n   171\t   (validate-call-site-coverage! tree frontend-metadata origin {}))\n   172\t  ([tree frontend-metadata origin\n   173\t    {:keys [declared? per-occurrence-origins?] :as _opts}]\n   174\t   (doseq [row frontend-metadata]\n   175\t     (when (and (marker-row? row) (not= 5 (count row)))\n   176\t       (throw (ex-info \"Malformed call-site marker row\"\n   177\t                       {:rule :yang/call-site-malformed, :row row}))))\n   178\t   (when declared?\n   179\t     (doseq [[row n] (frequencies (filter marker-row? frontend-metadata))]\n   180\t       (when (< 1 n)\n   181\t         (throw (ex-info \"Duplicate call-site marker in a declared table\"\n   182\t                         {:rule :yang/call-site-duplicate-entry,\n   183\t                          :site (vec (take 3 row)), :row row})))))\n   184\t   (let [{:keys [root rows]} tree\n   185\t         tag-at (into {}\n   186\t                      (map (fn [[r path id]] [[r path] (nth (get rows id) 1)]))\n   187\t                      (vm/occurrences tree))\n   188\t         eligible ((if per-occurrence-origins?\n   189\t                     (fn [_] (vm/application-occurrences tree))\n   190\t                     #(eligible-application-sites tree %))\n   191\t                   origin)\n   192\t         rows (filter (fn [row]\n   193\t                        (and (= 5 (count row)) (= call-site-key (nth row 3))))\n   194\t                      (distinct frontend-metadata))\n   195\t         by-site (group-by (fn [[o r path _ _]] [o r path]) rows)]\n   196\t    (doseq [[site srows] by-site]\n   197\t      (when (< 1 (count (distinct (map #(nth % 4) srows))))\n   198\t        (throw (ex-info \"Conflicting call-site marker values\"\n   199\t                        {:rule :yang/call-site-conflict, :site site,\n   200\t                         :values (vec (distinct (map #(nth % 4) srows)))}))))\n   201\t    ;; one occurrence — one [root-address path] — has exactly one\n   202\t    ;; origin (design §2.1); a second marker with a DIFFERENT, equally\n   203\t    ;; well-formed origin for an already-covered occurrence is a\n   204\t    ;; second claim to one fact and is rejected, not folded into the\n   205\t    ;; [root path] coverage projection. The one-origin-per-occurrence\n   206\t    ;; rule holds in EVERY validator mode; the default mode rejects a\n   207\t    ;; second claim with the same diagnostic (not a downstream\n   208\t    ;; nonexistent-path error) so the failure names the occurrence and\n   209\t    ;; both claims.\n   210\t    (doseq [[site srows] (group-by (fn [[_ r path]] [r path]) rows)]\n   211\t      (let [origins (distinct (map #(nth % 0) srows))]\n   212\t        (when (< 1 (count origins))\n   213\t          (throw (ex-info\n   214\t                   \"Call-site occurrence claimed by multiple origins\"\n   215\t                   {:rule :yang/call-site-multi-claim, :site site,\n   216\t                    :origins (vec (sort-by pr-str origins))})))))\n   217\t    (doseq [[o r path _ value] rows]\n   218\t      (when (not= call-site-version value)\n   219\t        (throw (ex-info \"Unsupported call-site marker version\"\n   220\t                        {:rule :yang/call-site-unsupported-version,\n   221\t                         :site [o r path], :value value})))\n   222\t      (when (and per-occurrence-origins? (not (vm/occurrence-origin? o)))\n   223\t        (throw (ex-info \"Call-site marker carries a malformed occurrence origin\"\n   224\t                        {:rule :yang/call-site-invalid-origin,\n   225\t                         :site [o r path], :origin o})))\n   226\t      (let [tag (when (and (= r root)\n   227\t                           (or per-occurrence-origins? (= o origin)))\n   228\t                  (get tag-at [r path]))]\n   229\t        (cond\n   230\t          (nil? tag)\n   231\t          (throw (ex-info \"Call-site marker names no occurrence\"\n   232\t                          {:rule :yang/call-site-nonexistent-path,\n   233\t                           :site [o r path]}))\n   234\t          (not= :application tag)\n   235\t          (throw (ex-info \"Call-site marker on a non-application occurrence\"\n   236\t                          {:rule :yang/call-site-non-application,\n   237\t                           :site [o r path], :tag tag})))))\n   238\t    (let [marked (if per-occurrence-origins?\n   239\t                   (into #{}\n   240\t                         (map (fn [[_ r path]] [r path]))\n   241\t                         (marked-application-sites frontend-metadata))\n   242\t                   (marked-application-sites frontend-metadata))]\n   243\t      (when (not= eligible marked)\n   244\t        (throw (ex-info \"Call-site coverage is not complete\"\n   245\t                        {:rule :yang/call-site-incomplete-coverage,\n   246\t                         :missing (vec (sort-by pr-str\n   247\t                                                (remove marked eligible))),\n   248\t                         :extra (vec (sort-by pr-str\n   249\t                                              (remove eligible marked)))}))))\n   250\t    true)))\n   251\t\n   252\t\n   253\t(defn validate-ast-call-sites!\n   254\t  \"Validate the C1 claim of a produced map AST `ast` under `origin`:\n   255\t   project it and compare the eligible application set derived from its\n   256\t   canonical rows with the marker set of its frontend-metadata side\n   257\t   table. The projected table is a declared canonical table, so it is\n   258\t   validated strictly (`:declared? true`). Returns true when the sets\n   259\t   are equal.\"\n   260\t  [ast origin]\n   261\t  (let [tree (vm/ast->semantic-bytecode ast)\n   262\t        tables (vm/ast-side-tables ast tree origin)]\n   263\t    (validate-call-site-coverage! tree (:frontend-metadata tables) origin\n   264\t                                  {:declared? true})))\n   265\t\n   266\t\n   267\t(defn literal?\n   268\t  \"Check if a value is a literal (self-evaluating).\"\n   269\t  [form]\n   270\t  (or (number? form)\n   271\t      (string? form)\n   272\t      (true? form)\n   273\t      (false? form)\n   274\t      (nil? form)\n   275\t      (keyword? form)\n   276\t      (vector? form)\n   277\t      (set? form)\n   278\t      (map? form)))\n    35\t\n    36\t\n    37\t(defn- diagnostic\n    38\t  \"The ex-data of the diagnostic lowering `src` throws, or nil.\"\n    39\t  [src]\n    40\t  (try (lower/lower-packet (parse src))\n    41\t       nil\n    42\t       (catch clojure.lang.ExceptionInfo e (ex-data e))))\n    43\t\n    44\t\n    45\t(defn- lines\n    46\t  \"What `run` prints: the logged lines, then an `Uncaught ...` line.\"\n    47\t  [{:js/keys [out uncaught]}]\n    48\t  (vec (concat out (when uncaught [(str \"Uncaught \" uncaught)]))))\n    49\t\n    50\t\n    51\t(defn- run-all\n    52\t  \"`src` lowered (bundled) and run on every VM: VM -> printed lines.\"\n    53\t  [src]\n    54\t  (let [ast (lower/lower-packet (parse src))]\n    55\t    (into {}\n    56\t          (map (fn [[k run]] [k (lines (render/output (run ast)))]))\n    57\t          parity/runners)))\n    58\t\n    59\t\n    60\t;; =============================================================================\n    61\t;; Goldens\n    62\t;; =============================================================================\n    63\t\n    64\t(defn- nodes\n    65\t  [tree]\n    66\t  (tree-seq #(or (map? %) (sequential? %))\n    67\t            #(if (map? %) (vals %) %)\n    68\t            tree))\n    69\t\n    70\t\n    71\t(defn- cells\n    72\t  \"`body` under one lambda over fresh cells: `[name init]` pairs. C1\n    73\t   finalized, as every tree the lowering answers now is\n    74\t   (`yang.typescript.antlr.lower`'s contract C1 block).\"\n    75\t  [pairs body]\n    76\t  (u/annotate-call-sites\n    77\t    (apply u/app\n    78\t           (u/lam (mapv (comp symbol first) pairs) body)\n    79\t           (map (fn [[_ init]] (u/app (u/v 'cell/new) init)) pairs))))\n    80\t\n    81\t\n    82\t(def ^:private undefined (u/lit :js/undefined))\n    83\t\n    84\t\n    85\t(defn- f64\n    86\t  [x]\n    87\t  (u/lit (cbor/float64 x)))\n    88\t\n    89\t\n    90\t(deftest var-declaration-golden-test\n    91\t  (is (= (cells [[\"x\" undefined]]\n    92\t                (u/then (u/then (u/app (u/v 'cell/set!) (u/v 'x) (f64 1.0))\n    93\t                                undefined)\n    94\t                        undefined))\n    95\t         (body \"var x = 1;\"))\n    96\t      \"a var cell starts undefined; the literal is float64 content\")\n    97\t  (is (= (cells [[\"y\" (u/lit :js/tdz)]]\n    98\t                (u/then (u/then (u/app (u/v 'cell/set!) (u/v 'y) (f64 2.0))\n    99\t                                undefined)\n   100\t                        undefined))\n   101\t         (body \"let y = 2;\"))\n   102\t      \"a let cell starts in TDZ\")\n   103\t  (is (= (cells [[\"z\" (u/lit :js/tdz)]]\n   104\t                (u/then (u/then (u/app (u/v 'cell/set!) (u/v 'z) undefined)\n   105\t                                undefined)\n   106\t                        undefined))\n   126\t    (is (contains? (reads \"1 + 2;\") 'js/add))))\n   127\t\n   128\t\n   129\t(deftest literal-golden-test\n   130\t  (is (= (f64 1.0) (nth (filter #(= (f64 1.0) %) (nodes (body \"1;\"))) 0))\n   131\t      \"the literal 1 is float64 content, never a bare integer\")\n   132\t  (is (= (u/lit 7) (first (filter #(= (u/lit 7) %) (nodes (body \"7n;\")))))\n   133\t      \"a BigInt literal is the bare exact integer\")\n   134\t  (is (some #(= (u/lit {:js/units [0xD800]}) %) (nodes (body \"'\\\\uD800';\")))\n   135\t      \"a lone surrogate literal is :js/units\")\n   136\t  (is (some #(= (u/lit {:js/str \"\\ud83d\\ude00\"}) %)\n   137\t            (nodes (body \"'\\\\uD83D\\\\uDE00';\")))\n   138\t      \"an escaped surrogate pair normalizes to :js/str\")\n   139\t  (is (some #(= (u/lit {:js/str \"a\"}) %) (nodes (body \"'a';\"))))\n   140\t  (is (some #(= (u/annotate-call-sites\n   141\t                  (u/app (u/v 'js/string->bigint)\n   142\t                         (u/lit {:js/str \"123456789012345678901234567890\"})))\n   143\t                %)\n   144\t            (nodes (body \"123456789012345678901234567890n;\")))\n   145\t      \"a BigInt past 2^53 - 1 is built by the guest\"))\n   146\t\n   147\t\n   148\t(deftest site-marks-test\n   149\t  (let [marks (fn [src]\n   150\t                (->> (nodes (lower/lower-packet (parse src)))\n   151\t                     (keep #(:yang/site (meta %)))\n   152\t                     frequencies))]\n   153\t    (is (= 1 (get (marks \"while (false) {}\") :loop)))\n   154\t    (is (= 2 (get (marks \"do {} while (false); for (;;) break;\") :loop)))\n   155\t    (is (some (fn [[k _]] (and (vector? k) (= :call (first k)) (= \"f\" (second k))))\n   156\t              (marks \"function f() {}\"))\n   157\t        \"a function body is a :call site\")))\n   158\t\n   159\t\n   160\t;; =============================================================================\n   161\t;; Semantics against Node\n   162\t;; =============================================================================\n   163\t\n   164\t(def ^:private node-table\n   165\t  \"[source printed-lines]: the lines Node prints for the source (with the\n   166\t   preload that prints an uncaught throw as an `Uncaught ...` line).\"\ntest/yang/typescript/antlr/lower_portable_test.cljc:206:(deftest hand-packet-golden-test\ntest/yang/typescript/antlr/linked_prelude_test.cljc:62:           (dissoc (last operands) :tail? :yang/call-site))\ntest/yang/typescript/antlr/lower_test.clj:91:  (is (= (cells [[\"x\" undefined]]\ntest/yang/typescript/antlr/lower_test.clj:97:  (is (= (cells [[\"y\" (u/lit :js/tdz)]]\ntest/yang/typescript/antlr/lower_test.clj:103:  (is (= (cells [[\"z\" (u/lit :js/tdz)]]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_18","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat docs/agents/roles/architect.md\nnl -ba docs/agents/team.md | sed -n '225,276p'\nnl -ba test/yang/typescript/antlr/lower_test.clj | sed -n '90,113p'\nnl -ba test/yang/typescript/antlr/linked_prelude_test.cljc | sed -n '44,84p'\nnl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/encoder.cljc | sed -n '104,181p;205,292p'\nrg -n 'call-site|call-sites|defn- call-site-claim' src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc | head -50\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_18","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat docs/agents/roles/architect.md\nnl -ba docs/agents/team.md | sed -n '225,276p'\nnl -ba test/yang/typescript/antlr/lower_test.clj | sed -n '90,113p'\nnl -ba test/yang/typescript/antlr/linked_prelude_test.cljc | sed -n '44,84p'\nnl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/encoder.cljc | sed -n '104,181p;205,292p'\nrg -n 'call-site|call-sites|defn- call-site-claim' src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc | head -50\"","aggregated_output":"---\ndescription: Lead System Architect role definition for datom.world\n---\n\n# ROLE: Lead System Architect\n\n## Domain Scope\n\n- Foundational axioms, architectural invariants, and design contracts\n- Subsystem boundaries, interpreters, host isolation, and explicit causality\n- Cross-platform architecture, migration strategy, and compatibility boundaries\n- ADR coherence, domain vocabulary, and theoretical grounding where useful\n- Architecture review for high-risk or cross-cutting changes\n- Commit sign-off: the sign-off on completed, review-reconciled work that\n  authorizes the orchestrator to stage, commit, merge, and push it\n  (trivial direct edits are exempt; see\n  [`orchestrator.md`](orchestrator.md#coordination-contract))\n\nThis role owns no permanent file list. Each task defines the artifacts it may\ninspect or change and any permitted expansion.\n\n## Core Responsibilities\n\n1. **Protect Invariants**: Strictly enforce the 6 non-negotiable invariants (no hidden global state, no implicit control flow, no raw callbacks, no shared mutable state, no layer collapsing, no assumed graphs).\n2. **Decompose Complexity**: When new requirements emerge, decompose them into append-only streams, explicit interpreters, and immutable datom representations.\n3. **Malleability Governance**: Ensure architecture adheres to bounded complexity, loose coupling, and high cohesion as defined in [`docs/agents/malleability.md`](../malleability.md).\n4. **Lineage Alignment**: Keep designs grounded in Plan 9 / Datomic / Lisp architectural lineage.\n\n## Delegation Prompt Template\n\n```text\nCreated-GMT: <YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS GMT>\nCreated-Local: <YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS local-timezone-name>\n\n# Task: <Task Name>\n\nRole: Lead System Architect\n\nImplementers:\n- Model: <model-name> | Assigned: <local timestamp> | Status: active | Rationale: <why>\n\nPerform a read-only architecture review of <design-change>.\n\nRead first:\n- docs/design/datom.world.md\n- <target-design-file>\n- <relevant-implementation-boundary>\n- <relevant-contract-tests>\n\nEvaluate foundational invariants, ownership boundaries, explicit state and\ncontrol flow, concurrency and linearization, dynamic extension, host isolation,\nCLJ/CLJS/CLJD portability, migration risk, completion criteria, and design\ncontradictions. Distinguish architectural defects from implementation gaps or\nintentionally deferred work. Do not edit files.\n\nBegin the final response exactly with:\nCompleted-GMT: <YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS GMT>\nCompleted-Local: <YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS local-timezone-name>\n\nThen report: severity | file:line | invariant/evidence | recommended correction.\nAlso confirm the requested properties that passed review.\n```\n   225\t|                             | live). Second choice when 3.8 capacity is throttled.               | work 3.8 can take; no measured advantage over it.                   |\n   226\t+-----------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------+\n   227\t| `qwen3.6-flash`             | Prior-generation Qwen fast tier (probed live).                     | Two generations old; lighter reasoning than either 3.8 tier.        |\n   228\t|                             |                                                                    | **Avoid for:** Anything the 3.8 lane can serve.                     |\n   229\t+-----------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------+\n   230\t| `deepseek-v4-pro` (qwen     | NOTE: the `qwen` lane's Token Plan ALSO serves `deepseek-v4-pro`   | Same-family collision: a deepseek-v4-pro author on the qwen lane    |\n   231\t| lane note)                  | (probed live 2026-11-04), in addition to the Qwen tiers.           | must NOT be reviewed by the DeepSeek lane (same family).            |\n   232\t+-----------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------+\n   233\t## Role Selection & Reviewer Independence\n   234\t\n   235\tThe Orchestrator is completely responsible for selecting the implementer for a given role. It dynamically\n   236\tcross-references the task's requirements against the **Model Strengths and Selection Guide** and the\n   237\t**Available Subscriptions & Cost Constraints**. Any model may fill any role provided its technical profile and\n   238\tcost align with the task.\n   239\t\n   240\t**Reviewer Independence Rules:**\n   241\tEvery change must be reviewed by a model from a **different family** to ensure\n   242\tindependent defect discovery. Never silently substitute a same-family reviewer.\n   243\tThe families represented in the Model Strengths table are: **Claude**,\n   244\t**DeepSeek**, **Gemini**, **GLM**, **GPT**, **Kimi**, **Mistral**,\n   245\t**Muse** (Meta), and **Qwen** (Alibaba). Family, not CLI, decides\n   246\tindependence: the `qwen` lane's `deepseek-v4-pro` is a **DeepSeek**\n   247\tauthor for review purposes, and Qwen-authored work (including anything\n   248\tby this interactive seat) must be reviewed by a different family.\n   249\tAny author from one family must be reviewed by a model from a different family.\n   250\t\n   251\tRoutine review applies only when independent; architectural or security review\n   252\tis mandatory when the role or risk requires it. For operational procedures, see\n   253\tthe [`Lead Engineering Orchestrator`](./roles/orchestrator.md).\n   254\t\n   255\t**Reviewer bench and parallel-lane scheduling** (2026-10-26 owner ruling,\n   256\tafter the jolt lane's throughput review):\n   257\t\n   258\t- **The standing reviewer bench** is wider than the implementation bench:\n   259\t  `kimi` (flat membership, native Kimi models only) joins the families above\n   260\t  as a standing review destination. The independence rule is unchanged: the\n   261\t  reviewer must be a different model family from the author.\n   262\t- **Parallel-lane scheduling**: when slice N lands on its branch, slice N+1's\n   263\t  implementation dispatches immediately and slice N's review runs\n   264\t  concurrently. Gate: review N must complete **before slice N+1 merges** — a\n   265\t  defect found in N's review must still be fixable without N+1 having built\n   266\t  on it. Judgment is required on what N+1 actually built on; tightly-coupled\n   267\t  slices serialize.\n   268\t- **Shared ledgers scale with concurrency**: the pre-push row-count check on\n   269\t  append-only ledgers (`docs/agents/known-gaps.md`; orchestrator.md Workflow\n   270\t  step 10) is more important under parallel review, not less — parallel\n   271\t  review means parallel merges (the 2026-10-25 corruption precedent:\n   272\t  merge 4d6fd818 silently dropped ~66 ledger rows by replacing the file).\n   273\t- Never relax the independence rule or skip reviews on small slices; the fix\n   274\t  for throughput is more reviewers, not fewer reviews.\n    90\t(deftest var-declaration-golden-test\n    91\t  (is (= (cells [[\"x\" undefined]]\n    92\t                (u/then (u/then (u/app (u/v 'cell/set!) (u/v 'x) (f64 1.0))\n    93\t                                undefined)\n    94\t                        undefined))\n    95\t         (body \"var x = 1;\"))\n    96\t      \"a var cell starts undefined; the literal is float64 content\")\n    97\t  (is (= (cells [[\"y\" (u/lit :js/tdz)]]\n    98\t                (u/then (u/then (u/app (u/v 'cell/set!) (u/v 'y) (f64 2.0))\n    99\t                                undefined)\n   100\t                        undefined))\n   101\t         (body \"let y = 2;\"))\n   102\t      \"a let cell starts in TDZ\")\n   103\t  (is (= (cells [[\"z\" (u/lit :js/tdz)]]\n   104\t                (u/then (u/then (u/app (u/v 'cell/set!) (u/v 'z) undefined)\n   105\t                                undefined)\n   106\t                        undefined))\n   107\t         (body \"let z;\"))\n   108\t      \"a let without initializer leaves TDZ with undefined\"))\n   109\t\n   110\t\n   111\t(deftest read-golden-test\n   112\t  (let [reads (fn [src]\n   113\t                (->> (nodes (body src))\n    44\t             (= :application (:type node))\n    45\t             (= 'yin/def (get-in node [:operator :name])))\n    46\t    (get-in node [:operands 0 :value])))\n    47\t\n    48\t\n    49\t;; =============================================================================\n    50\t;; The module emitters\n    51\t;; =============================================================================\n    52\t\n    53\t(deftest jssp-module-uast-is-one-wide-application-test\n    54\t  (let [ast hooks/module-uast\n    55\t        operands (:operands ast)\n    56\t        definitions (butlast operands)]\n    57\t    (is (= :application (:type ast)))\n    58\t    (is (= :lambda (:type (:operator ast))))\n    59\t    (is (= (count operands) (count (:params (:operator ast)))))\n    60\t    (is (nil? (get-in ast [:operator :body :value])))\n    61\t    (is (= (u/sexp->uast '(require (quote js)))\n    62\t           (dissoc (last operands) :tail? :yang/call-site))\n    63\t        \"the delivered require, minus its tail mark and its C1 marker\")\n    64\t    (testing \"the placeholders come first, each the literal :js/uninit\"\n    65\t      (let [n (count hooks/runtime-keys)\n    66\t            placeholders (take n definitions)]\n    67\t        (is (= (mapv hooks/strip hooks/runtime-keys)\n    68\t               (mapv def-key placeholders)))\n    69\t        (is (every? #(= {:type :literal, :value :js/uninit}\n    70\t                        (dissoc (get-in % [:operands 1]) :tail?))\n    71\t                    placeholders))))\n    72\t    (testing \"then every definition, stripped, in definition order\"\n    73\t      (is (= (mapv (comp hooks/strip first) hooks/function-definitions)\n    74\t             (mapv def-key (drop (count hooks/runtime-keys) definitions)))))\n    75\t    (testing \"no symbol of the module's own namespace survives stripping\"\n    76\t      (is (not-any? (fn [x] (and (symbol? x) (= \"js.sp\" (namespace x))))\n    77\t                    (tree-seq coll? seq ast))))\n    78\t    (testing \"`js/*` references stay qualified: the base prelude's exports\"\n    79\t      (is (some (fn [x] (and (symbol? x) (= \"js\" (namespace x))))\n    80\t                (tree-seq coll? seq ast))))))\n    81\t\n    82\t\n    83\t(deftest jssp-module-exports-test\n    84\t  (is (= (set (map (comp hooks/strip first) hooks/function-definitions))\n   104\t\n   105\t\n   106\t(defn- project-member\n   107\t  [member origin member-index]\n   108\t  (cond\n   109\t    (and (map? member) (contains? member :type))\n   110\t    (let [tree (vm/ast->semantic-bytecode member)]\n   111\t      (merge {:tree tree, :entity-occurrences []}\n   112\t             (vm/ast-side-tables member tree origin)))\n   113\t\n   114\t    (and (map? member) (contains? member :root) (contains? member :rows))\n   115\t    (let [metadata (:frontend-metadata member)]\n   116\t      (when (and (some? metadata) (not (sequential? metadata)))\n   117\t        (throw (ex-info \"Supplied frontend-metadata is not a row sequence\"\n   118\t                        {:rule :frontend-metadata, :member-index member-index,\n   119\t                         :metadata metadata})))\n   120\t      (check-projected-claim! metadata member)\n   121\t      {:tree member,\n   122\t       :source-positions (vec (or (:source-positions member) [])),\n   123\t       :frontend-metadata (vec (or metadata [])),\n   124\t       :entity-occurrences []})\n   125\t\n   126\t    (sequential? member)\n   127\t    (let [datoms (vec member)\n   128\t          ast (vm/datoms->ast datoms)\n   129\t          tree (vm/ast->semantic-bytecode ast)]\n   130\t      (merge {:tree tree\n   131\t              :entity-occurrences (datom-entity-occurrences datoms member-index)}\n   132\t             (vm/ast-side-tables ast tree origin)))\n   133\t\n   134\t    :else\n   135\t    (throw (ex-info \"Unsupported source batch member\"\n   136\t                    {:rule :batch-member, :member member,\n   137\t                     :member-index member-index}))))\n   138\t\n   139\t\n   140\t(defn- project-envelope\n   141\t  [{:yin/keys [source-medium batch-token batch root] :as envelope}]\n   142\t  (when-not (and (vector? batch)\n   143\t                 (seq batch)\n   144\t                 (integer? root)\n   145\t                 (<= 0 root)\n   146\t                 (< root (count batch)))\n   147\t    (throw (ex-info \"Malformed source batch envelope\"\n   148\t                    {:rule :batch-envelope, :envelope envelope})))\n   149\t  (let [projected (mapv (fn [j member]\n   150\t                          (project-member member\n   151\t                                          (vm/source-origin source-medium\n   152\t                                                            batch-token j)\n   153\t                                          j))\n   154\t                        (range) batch)]\n   155\t    (assoc envelope\n   156\t           :yin/batch (mapv :tree projected)\n   157\t           :yin/source-positions (into [] (mapcat :source-positions) projected)\n   158\t           :yin/frontend-metadata (into [] (mapcat :frontend-metadata) projected)\n   159\t           :yin/entity-occurrences (into [] (mapcat :entity-occurrences) projected))))\n   160\t\n   161\t\n   162\t(defn project\n   163\t  \"One program-medium batch to its canonical row set `{:root id, :rows …}`\n   164\t   (§6.1). A batch that is neither a map AST nor a datom batch is a defect\n   165\t   of the medium and throws here, at the boundary, naming where it failed.\"\n   166\t  [batch]\n   167\t  (cond\n   168\t    (and (map? batch) (contains? batch :yin/batch))\n   169\t    (project-envelope batch)\n   170\t\n   171\t    (map? batch) (vm/ast->semantic-bytecode batch)\n   172\t    :else (datoms->rows batch)))\n   173\t\n   174\t\n   175\t;; =============================================================================\n   176\t;; The macro expander's input batch (yin.vm.macro.md §2.1, §10.2)\n   177\t;; =============================================================================\n   178\t\n   179\t(defn- definition-name\n   180\t  \"The name of a `(yin/def <literal-symbol> value)` AST node (§2.2), else nil.\"\n   181\t  [{:keys [type operator operands]}]\n   205\t\n   206\t\n   207\t(defn- declaration-order\n   208\t  \"§3.5's declaration order for one node's children: for an application\n   209\t   whose operator is a lambda, the operands left to right and then the\n   210\t   lambda body (two coordinates below the application); otherwise grammar\n   211\t   order.\"\n   212\t  [node]\n   213\t  (let [places (ast-children node)]\n   214\t    (if (and (= :application (:type node)) (= :lambda (:type (:operator node))))\n   215\t      (concat (rest places) [[[2 3] (:body (:operator node))]])\n   216\t      places)))\n   217\t\n   218\t\n   219\t(defn- definition-occurrences\n   220\t  \"Every definition occurrence of one member AST as `{:path p :declared? b}`,\n   221\t   in source declaration order. A declared occurrence is one whose value is\n   222\t   a lambda the frontend flagged `:macro?`.\"\n   223\t  [ast]\n   224\t  (letfn [(walk [node path]\n   225\t            (concat (when (definition-name node)\n   226\t                      [{:path path,\n   227\t                        :declared? (boolean (:macro? (second (:operands node))))}])\n   228\t                    (mapcat (fn [[suffix child]] (walk child (into path suffix)))\n   229\t                            (declaration-order node))))]\n   230\t    (vec (walk ast []))))\n   231\t\n   232\t\n   233\t(defn- member-ast\n   234\t  [member]\n   235\t  (cond (and (map? member) (contains? member :type)) member\n   236\t        (sequential? member) (vm/datoms->ast (vec member))\n   237\t        :else (throw (ex-info \"Unsupported program batch member\"\n   238\t                              {:rule :batch-member, :member member}))))\n   239\t\n   240\t\n   241\t(def ^:private call-site-key\n   242\t  \"The reserved frontend-metadata key of the call-site occurrence\n   243\t   contract C1 (`yang.clojure`), enforced at this boundary but not\n   244\t   owned by it.\"\n   245\t  :yang/call-site)\n   246\t\n   247\t\n   248\t(defn- marked-call-sites\n   249\t  \"The `[path value]` of every node of map AST `ast` carrying the C1\n   250\t   key, walked by the row grammar. Literal payloads are data, never\n   251\t   syntax, and are not walked. Member ASTs are already projected by the\n   252\t   time this runs, so every tag is a grammar tag.\"\n   253\t  [ast]\n   254\t  (letfn [(walk\n   255\t            [node path]\n   256\t            (into (if (contains? node call-site-key)\n   257\t                    [[path (get node call-site-key)]]\n   258\t                    [])\n   259\t                  (mapcat (fn [[j [field kind]]]\n   260\t                            (let [pos (+ j 2)\n   261\t                                  value (get node field)]\n   262\t                              (case kind\n   263\t                                :node (walk value (conj path pos))\n   264\t                                :nodes (mapcat (fn [[i child]]\n   265\t                                                 (walk child\n   266\t                                                       (conj path [pos i])))\n   267\t                                               (map-indexed vector value))\n   268\t                                nil)))\n   269\t                          (map-indexed vector\n   270\t                                       (get vm/semantic-bytecode-grammar\n   271\t                                            (:type node))))))]\n   272\t    (walk ast [])))\n   273\t\n   274\t\n   275\t(defn- check-call-site-claim!\n   276\t  \"Refuse a batch member whose C1 markers do not exactly cover its\n   277\t   projected tree, naming the failed `:rule`: canonical-row production\n   278\t   must not silently drop a frontend's coverage claim. The claim is\n   279\t   checked root-relatively — admission origins belong to the admitting\n   280\t   expander, not to this projection. A member carrying no markers\n   281\t   makes no claim and passes; the executed tree's table is finalized\n   282\t   after expansion, over the final rows. Answers true when the member\n   283\t   claimed coverage (it passed the check), false when it carried no\n   284\t   markers — one verdict per member, so the selected member's own\n   285\t   verdict, never a sibling's, decides whether the expander finalizes\n   286\t   its side table.\"\n   287\t  [ast tree]\n   288\t  (let [marked (marked-call-sites ast)]\n   289\t    (if (seq marked)\n   290\t      (do (doseq [[path value] marked]\n   291\t            (when (not= 1 value)\n   292\t              (throw (ex-info \"Unsupported call-site marker version\"\n25:(declare recovered-call-site-claim sequenced-wrapper-paths)\n100:;; A module whose frontend finalized its tree (`:yang/call-site 1` on\n106:;; (`:yang.call-site/manifest`), beside the tree root, the publication's\n110:;; through the `publish-module!` result's `:call-sites`, not through\n183:(defn- claims-call-sites?\n188:  (boolean (some #(= :yang/call-site %) (tree-seq coll? seq ast))))\n191:(defn- call-site-claim\n200:  (when (claims-call-sites? ast)\n202:          extracted (filter #(= :yang/call-site (nth % 3))\n289:                (if (contains? spec :call-site-rows)\n290:                  (recovered-call-site-claim (:call-site-rows spec)\n291:                                              (:call-site-wrappers spec)\n293:                                                   :call-site-wrappers-evidence\n296:                  (call-site-claim ast tree admission)))]\n315:      (refusal :yin.link.publish/unsupported-call-site-version claim)\n321:      (refusal :yin.link.publish/incomplete-call-site-coverage claim)\n386:            call-sites (when (:rows claim)\n409:                               record {:yang.call-site/schema 1\n410:                                       :yang.call-site/manifest address\n411:                                       :yang.call-site/root (:root tree)\n412:                                       :yang.call-site/origin (:origin claim)\n413:                                       :yang.call-site/table table\n414:                                       :yang.call-site/provenance provenance}]\n439:              call-sites (assoc :call-sites call-sites))))))))\n487:(defn published-call-site-table\n491:   names the manifest (`:yang.call-site/manifest`); the manifest never\n494:   `publish-module!` result map (whose `:call-sites :record` and\n497:   only when its schema is 1, its `:yang.call-site/manifest` is the\n498:   manifest in question, its `:yang.call-site/root` is that manifest's\n500:   (`:yang.call-site/origin`, held to be a well-formed occurrence\n506:     (published-call-site-table handle\n509:                                        [:call-sites :record]))\n510:     (published-call-site-table handle nil record-or-result)))\n515:                  (= 1 (:yang.call-site/schema record))\n516:                  (jing/segment-address? (:yang.call-site/manifest record))\n518:                      (= manifest-address (:yang.call-site/manifest record)))\n519:                  (jing/segment-address? (:yang.call-site/table record))\n520:                  (vm/occurrence-origin? (:yang.call-site/origin record)))\n522:                                  (:yang.call-site/manifest record) nil)]\n524:                      (= (:yang.call-site/root record)\n528:                                           (:yang.call-site/table record)\n531:                   {:origin (:yang.call-site/origin record),\n546:   `published-call-site-table`. The relation lives OUTSIDE the\n554:                                               [:call-sites :record]))\n560:                  (= 1 (:yang.call-site/schema record))\n561:                  (jing/segment-address? (:yang.call-site/manifest record))\n563:                      (= manifest-address (:yang.call-site/manifest record)))\n564:                  (jing/segment-address? (:yang.call-site/provenance record)))\n566:                                  (:yang.call-site/manifest record) nil)]\n568:                      (= (:yang.call-site/root record)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
