{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_19","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm.cljc | sed -n '1010,1055p'\nnl -ba src/cljc/yang/typescript/antlr/prelude.cljc | sed -n '4280,4407p'\nnl -ba test/yang/typescript/antlr/linked_harness.cljc | sed -n '48,84p'\nnl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc | sed -n '98,115p;183,228p;378,438p'\nnl -ba /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/yang-typescript/1794514249000-engineer-ts-callsite-adoption.qwen3.8-max.findings.md | sed -n '122,155p;360,408p;414,462p'\"","aggregated_output":"  1010\t\n  1011\t;; =============================================================================\n  1012\t;; Semantic bytecode: flat content-addressed rows\n  1013\t;; =============================================================================\n  1014\t;; docs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md §2. One row `[id tag & slots]` per\n  1015\t;; distinct node; `id` is `(jing/segment-key [tag & slots])`.\n  1016\t\n  1017\t(def semantic-bytecode-grammar\n  1018\t  \"The Universal AST row-slot table (yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md §2.3):\n  1019\t   tag -> ordered `[field kind]` slots, rather than executable bytecode. Position `i` of a\n  1020\t   row body (after the tag) holds the map field named at `i`, so this one\n  1021\t   table drives both projection and reconstruction.\"\n  1022\t  {:literal [[:value :data]],\n  1023\t   :variable [[:name :sym]],\n  1024\t   :lambda [[:params :syms] [:body :node]],\n  1025\t   :application [[:operator :node] [:operands :nodes] [:tail? :bool]],\n  1026\t   :if [[:test :node] [:consequent :node] [:alternate :node]],\n  1027\t   :dao.stream.apply/call [[:op :kw] [:operands :nodes]],\n  1028\t   :vm/gensym [[:prefix :str]],\n  1029\t   :vm/store-get [[:key :key]],\n  1030\t   :vm/store-put [[:key :key] [:val :data]],\n  1031\t   :vm/current-continuation [],\n  1032\t   :vm/park [],\n  1033\t   :vm/resume [[:parked-id :kw] [:val :node]],\n  1034\t   :stream/make [[:buffer :int]],\n  1035\t   :stream/put [[:target :node] [:val :node]],\n  1036\t   :stream/cursor [[:source :node]],\n  1037\t   :stream/next [[:source :node]],\n  1038\t   :stream/close [[:source :node]]})\n  1039\t\n  1040\t\n  1041\t(def ^:private semantic-bytecode-defaults\n  1042\t  \"§2.4 saturation: `[tag field]` -> the default written map→rows. rows→map\n  1043\t   never re-defaults; a nil in one of these slots is a defect.\"\n  1044\t  {[:vm/gensym :prefix] \"id\",\n  1045\t   [:stream/make :buffer] default-stream-capacity,\n  1046\t   [:application :tail?] false,\n  1047\t   [:application :operands] [],\n  1048\t   [:dao.stream.apply/call :operands] []})\n  1049\t\n  1050\t\n  1051\t(defn- strip-symbol-meta\n  1052\t  \"§2.5: reader metadata on names is frontend metadata, not content.\"\n  1053\t  [x]\n  1054\t  (if (symbol? x) (with-meta x nil) x))\n  1055\t\n  4280\t         out))]\n  4281\t   ['js/args-spread\n  4282\t    '(fn [args value]\n  4283\t       (if (js/array? value)\n  4284\t         (data/into args\n  4285\t                    (js/spread-array-items (get (cell/get value) :items) 0 []))\n  4286\t         (js/throw-type-error {:js/str \"Spread value is not iterable\"})))]])\n  4287\t\n  4288\t\n  4289\t(def definitions\n  4290\t  \"The single definition list, `[store-key form]` in definition order:\n  4291\t   every prelude function, the literal state slot, then `js/init!`.\n  4292\t   Defining them runs nothing.\"\n  4293\t  (into (into (into (into (into (into core-definitions object-definitions)\n  4294\t                                t4-definitions)\n  4295\t                          array-definitions)\n  4296\t                    json-definitions)\n  4297\t              class-definitions)\n  4298\t        [['js.rt/state :js/uninit] ['js/init! (init-form)]]))\n  4299\t\n  4300\t\n  4301\t(def ^:private linked-definitions\n  4302\t  \"The `js` module body; the common call runtime is pinned as a requirement.\"\n  4303\t  definitions)\n  4304\t\n  4305\t\n  4306\t(defn- definitions->uast\n  4307\t  [defs]\n  4308\t  ;; A linear `then` chain adds two tree levels per definition and can\n  4309\t  ;; overflow the host printer's stack. Balance the sequence, preserving\n  4310\t  ;; left-to-right effects and the last definition's value.\n  4311\t  (letfn [(sequence-tree\n  4312\t            [nodes]\n  4313\t            (if (<= (count nodes) 1)\n  4314\t              (first nodes)\n  4315\t              (let [middle (quot (count nodes) 2)]\n  4316\t                (u/then (sequence-tree (subvec nodes 0 middle))\n  4317\t                        (sequence-tree (subvec nodes middle))))))]\n  4318\t    (sequence-tree (mapv (fn [[k form]] (u/def! k (u/sexp->uast form))) defs))))\n  4319\t\n  4320\t\n  4321\t(def functions-uast\n  4322\t  \"The shared calling runtime followed by every js definition. Defining\n  4323\t   them runs nothing, so this loads on any composition, with or without cells.\"\n  4324\t  (definitions->uast (into call/definitions definitions)))\n  4325\t\n  4326\t\n  4327\t(def uast\n  4328\t  \"The bundled prelude: every definition, then the task's runtime state\n  4329\t   allocated by `js/init!`.\"\n  4330\t  (u/then functions-uast (u/sexp->uast '(js/init!))))\n  4331\t\n  4332\t\n  4333\t;; =============================================================================\n  4334\t;; The linked js module requires the separately published `yang.call` module\n  4335\t;; =============================================================================\n  4336\t\n  4337\t(def module-name\n  4338\t  \"The linker module the JavaScript runtime profile is published as.\"\n  4339\t  'js)\n  4340\t\n  4341\t\n  4342\t(def runtime-keys\n  4343\t  \"Every key `js/init!` allocates, the ready flag aside, sorted.\"\n  4344\t  (vec (sort-by str\n  4345\t                (concat '[js.rt/ctx js.rt/out js.rt/global js.rt/obj-proto\n  4346\t                          js.rt/fn-proto js.rt/symbol-proto js.rt/array-proto]\n  4347\t                        (map second error-classes)\n  4348\t                        (map first primitive-protos)))))\n  4349\t\n  4350\t\n  4351\t(defn strip\n  4352\t  \"`sym` without the module's own namespace `js`; any other value as it\n  4353\t   is. `js.rt/*` stays qualified: an internal store key.\"\n  4354\t  [sym]\n  4355\t  (core/strip \"js\" sym))\n  4356\t\n  4357\t\n  4358\t(def ^:private module-definitions\n  4359\t  \"The module's definition list: a `:js/uninit` placeholder for every\n  4360\t   runtime key, then every definition, stripped.\"\n  4361\t  (core/module-definitions \"js\" :js/uninit runtime-keys linked-definitions))\n  4362\t\n  4363\t\n  4364\t(def module-uast\n  4365\t  \"The module tree: one application whose operands are the definitions, in\n  4366\t   order, applied to a lambda that returns nil. C1 finalized, like every\n  4367\t   published production tree: its `:yang/call-site` markers publish beside\n  4368\t   its manifest (see `yin.vm.linker.publish`), never inside it, so the\n  4369\t   manifest keeps schema 1 and its address does not move.\"\n  4370\t  (u/annotate-call-sites (core/module-tree module-definitions [])))\n  4371\t\n  4372\t\n  4373\t(def module-exports\n  4374\t  \"The module's exports: every `js/` key of the definition list, stripped.\"\n  4375\t  (core/exports \"js\" definitions))\n  4376\t\n  4377\t\n  4378\t(def free-names\n  4379\t  \"Every variable name some occurrence of the map AST reads unbound by an\n  4380\t   enclosing lambda.\"\n  4381\t  core/free-names)\n  4382\t\n  4383\t\n  4384\t(def defined-keys\n  4385\t  \"Every literal key the map AST defines with `yin/def`, at any depth.\"\n  4386\t  core/defined-keys)\n  4387\t\n  4388\t\n  4389\t(def ^:private module-free-names\n  4390\t  \"The names the module tree reads and does not define, sorted: the\n  4391\t   primitives and the host exports its manifest must declare.\"\n  4392\t  (core/free-name-vec module-uast))\n  4393\t\n  4394\t\n  4395\t(defn module-spec\n  4396\t  \"`yin.vm.linker.publish/publish-module!`'s spec for the module `js` over\n  4397\t   the host registry `registry`, pinned to the published `yang.call` module\n  4398\t   at `call-address`. A free name nothing supplies is refused before\n  4399\t   anything is published. This namespace emits; it never publishes.\"\n  4400\t  [registry call-address]\n  4401\t  (core/module-spec {:module-name module-name,\n  4402\t                     :ast module-uast,\n  4403\t                     :exports module-exports,\n  4404\t                     :requires {'yang.call call-address},\n  4405\t                     :free-names module-free-names,\n  4406\t                     :skip? #(= \"yang.call\" (namespace %)),\n  4407\t                     :registry registry,\n    48\t   (-> (module/default-registry)\n    49\t       module/register-cell-module\n    50\t       (data/register-data-module {::data/max-items 1048576})\n    51\t       (prelude/register-integer-module limits)\n    52\t       module/register-stream-module)))\n    53\t\n    54\t\n    55\t(def published\n    56\t  \"`js` published once into its own content store:\n    57\t   `{:store s :result r :address a :call-address ca}`. `yang.call` is\n    58\t   published first so `js` pins its shared calling runtime.\"\n    59\t  (delay\n    60\t    (let [store (mem/create-content-mem)\n    61\t          call-result (publish/publish-module! store (call/module-spec (registry)))\n    62\t          result (publish/publish-module! store\n    63\t                                          (prelude/module-spec (registry)\n    64\t                                                               (:address call-result)))]\n    65\t      {:store store,\n    66\t       :result result,\n    67\t       :address (:address result),\n    68\t       :call-address (:address call-result)})))\n    69\t\n    70\t\n    71\t(def published-jssp\n    72\t  \"`jssp` published once into `js`'s own content store, which its pinned\n    73\t   requirement already lives in: the same shape as `published`.\"\n    74\t  (delay\n    75\t    (let [{:keys [store address]} @published\n    76\t          result (publish/publish-module!\n    77\t                   store (safepoint/module-spec (registry) address))]\n    78\t      {:store store, :result result, :address (:address result)})))\n    79\t\n    80\t\n    81\t(defn source\n    82\t  \"The serving composition over the published store: `name-env` defaults\n    83\t   to `{js <address> yang.call <address>}`, derivation `:trusted`, the test\n    84\t   being the publisher. `jssp`-serving sources pass their own `name-env`.\"\n    98\t;; =============================================================================\n    99\t;;\n   100\t;; A module whose frontend finalized its tree (`:yang/call-site 1` on\n   101\t;; every final `:application` occurrence) publishes its frontend-metadata\n   102\t;; side table beside its manifest: the manifest keeps the closed\n   103\t;; schema-1 key set (a manifest address names code, and nothing else),\n   104\t;; so the side table never enters the hashed manifest. The manifest is\n   105\t;; materialized first, and the publication record then names it\n   106\t;; (`:yang.call-site/manifest`), beside the tree root, the publication's\n   107\t;; recorded admission origin, and the table's address — a record names\n   108\t;; a manifest, never the reverse (the site-set precedent,\n   109\t;; `yang.python.antlr.siteset`). Custody of the record and table runs\n   110\t;; through the `publish-module!` result's `:call-sites`, not through\n   111\t;; the module closure: execution never consults C1 tables, so the\n   112\t;; closure walker does not follow them. The publication's origin is an ADMISSION identity\n   113\t;; (design §2.1): a token the composition pins explicitly, draws from\n   114\t;; a composition-owned scope object, or — by default — has derived\n   115\t;; from the publication specification's own durable identity; no\n   183\t(defn- claims-call-sites?\n   184\t  \"True when map AST `ast` carries the C1 key anywhere. A hit inside a\n   185\t   literal payload is data, not a claim: extraction then finds no\n   186\t   markers and the module publishes unannotated, as it should.\"\n   187\t  [ast]\n   188\t  (boolean (some #(= :yang/call-site %) (tree-seq coll? seq ast))))\n   189\t\n   190\t\n   191\t(defn- call-site-claim\n   192\t  \"The C1 claim `ast` makes over its canonical `tree`: nil when it\n   193\t   carries no markers; `{:origin o :rows [...]}` in canonical-byte\n   194\t   order (`jing/canonical-compare`) when the extracted markers exactly cover the tree's eligible\n   195\t   application occurrences; `{:missing [...] :extra [...]}` when they\n   196\t   do not; `{:unsupported-version v :path p}` when a marker's value is\n   197\t   not version 1 — a claim rejection, never a silent acceptance of a\n   198\t   table a retriever would read as version 1.\"\n   199\t  [ast tree admission]\n   200\t  (when (claims-call-sites? ast)\n   201\t    (let [origin (publication-origin admission)\n   202\t          extracted (filter #(= :yang/call-site (nth % 3))\n   203\t                            (:frontend-metadata\n   204\t                              (vm/ast-side-tables ast tree origin)))\n   205\t          eligible (into #{}\n   206\t                         (map (fn [[r p]] [origin r p]))\n   207\t                         (vm/application-occurrences tree))\n   208\t          marked (into #{}\n   209\t                       (map (fn [[o r p _ _]] [o r p]))\n   210\t                       extracted)]\n   211\t      (or (when-let [[v p] (some (fn [row]\n   212\t                                   (let [v (nth row 4)]\n   213\t                                     (when (not (and (integer? v) (= 1 v)))\n   214\t                                       [v (subvec row 0 3)])))\n   215\t                                 extracted)]\n   216\t            {:unsupported-version v, :path p})\n   217\t          (if (= eligible marked)\n   218\t            {:origin origin, :rows (vec (sort jing/canonical-compare extracted))}\n   219\t            {:missing (vec (sort jing/canonical-compare (remove marked eligible))),\n   220\t             :extra (vec (sort jing/canonical-compare (remove eligible marked)))})))))\n   221\t\n   222\t\n   223\t(defn link-local\n   224\t  \"Link `format`'s image through the manifest `address` over `handle`'s\n   225\t   own content, `:verifying` with discharge deferred, as a serving\n   226\t   composition does (yin.vm.linker.dht.md 4.1): a fresh local runtime per\n   227\t   call, so no request reaches any peer.  `opts` overrides the link\n   228\t   options; its `:bounds` are the runtime's composition bounds (section\n   378\t                      (into {} (map (fn [[n p]] [n (:yin.k/profile p)])\n   379\t                                    primitives))\n   380\t                      :yin.module/footprint fp}\n   381\t            address (jing/materialize! handle manifest)\n   382\t            ;; the C1 side table and its publication record, beside\n   383\t            ;; the manifest: the record names the manifest (a record\n   384\t            ;; names a manifest, never the reverse), so each admission\n   385\t            ;; of one specification keeps its own record and table\n   386\t            call-sites (when (:rows claim)\n   387\t                         (let [table (jing/materialize! handle (:rows claim))\n   388\t                               ;; cc3 item 3: the instruction-provenance\n   389\t                               ;; relation of all three images, persisted\n   390\t                               ;; as a side artifact OUTSIDE the schema-1\n   391\t                               ;; manifest hash (the record names it; the\n   392\t                               ;; manifest never names the record)\n   393\t                               provenance (jing/materialize!\n   394\t                                            handle\n   395\t                                            {:yin.vm.provenance/schema 1\n   396\t                                             :yin.vm.provenance/root (:root tree)\n   397\t                                             :yin.vm.provenance/semantic\n   398\t                                             (mapv (fn [[pc o r p]]\n   399\t                                                     [sem pc o r p])\n   400\t                                                   (:call-provenance sem-proj))\n   401\t                                             :yin.vm.provenance/stack\n   402\t                                             (mapv (fn [row]\n   403\t                                                     (assoc row 0 h-address))\n   404\t                                                   (:call-provenance stack-full))\n   405\t                                             :yin.vm.provenance/register\n   406\t                                             (mapv (fn [row]\n   407\t                                                     (assoc row 0 r-address))\n   408\t                                                   (:call-provenance register-full))})\n   409\t                               record {:yang.call-site/schema 1\n   410\t                                       :yang.call-site/manifest address\n   411\t                                       :yang.call-site/root (:root tree)\n   412\t                                       :yang.call-site/origin (:origin claim)\n   413\t                                       :yang.call-site/table table\n   414\t                                       :yang.call-site/provenance provenance}]\n   415\t                           {:record (jing/materialize! handle record)\n   416\t                            :table table\n   417\t                            :provenance provenance\n   418\t                            :origin (:origin claim)\n   419\t                            :root (:root tree)\n   420\t                            :manifest address}))\n   421\t            walked (closure/walk handle address opts)]\n   422\t        (if (not= :complete (:yin.link.closure/outcome walked))\n   423\t          (refusal :yin.link.publish/incomplete-closure\n   424\t                   {:address address :walk walked})\n   425\t          (let [links (into {}\n   426\t                            (map (fn [f]\n   427\t                                   [(:format f)\n   428\t                                    (link-local handle address f\n   429\t                                                (select-keys opts\n   430\t                                                             [:bounds]))]))\n   431\t                            code-formats)]\n   432\t            (cond-> {:address address :manifest manifest\n   433\t                     :identities {:yin.semantic/code sem\n   434\t                                  :yin.debruijn.code sem\n   435\t                                  :yin.debruijn.register sem}\n   436\t                     :checksums {:yin.debruijn.code h\n   437\t                                 :yin.debruijn.register r}\n   438\t                     :links links}\n   122\t\n   123\tSix files touched: three production, three existing-test repairs, plus one new test\n   124\tnamespace. **Nothing under `src/cljc/yang/core/`, `src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc`, or\n   125\t`src/cljc/yin/` was edited** — the generic core was consumed read-only, as bounded.\n   126\t\n   127\t### 1.1 Production (the adoption)\n   128\t\n   129\t| File | Lines | Change |\n   130\t|---|---|---|\n   131\t| `src/cljc/yang/typescript/antlr/lower.cljc` | **2262-2289** | New `;; Call-site occurrence contract C1 (Addendum A, design §2)` block: the reserved key + version, the coordinate tuple `[origin root-address path :yang/call-site 1]`, the projection rule (the key drops out of canonical rows into the EXISTING generic frontend-metadata side table), the three-way distinction from `:yang/site` **and** from the exception track's `cell/dsg__new-provenance` / `cell/dsg__provenance` family, and the all-or-nothing coverage rule that motivates the `lower-unit*` seam. |\n   132\t| | **2291-2296** | `lower-module-body` → `(u/annotate-call-sites (module-body (context packet)))`; docstring + \"C1 finalized\". |\n   133\t| | **2299-2306** | **NEW** `defn- lower-unit*` — the unmarked seam; body is the old `lower-unit` body verbatim. |\n   134\t| | **2308-2314** | `lower-unit` → `(u/annotate-call-sites (lower-unit* packet))`. |\n   135\t| | **2329-2345** | `lower-units`: `mapv lower-unit` → `mapv lower-unit*`; return is `(u/annotate-call-sites (with-runtime prelude main))`. |\n   136\t| | **2347-2361** | `lower-packet`: `(lower-unit packet)` → `(lower-unit* packet)`; return is `(u/annotate-call-sites (with-runtime prelude main))`; docstring notes C1 finalization. |\n   137\t| | *2371-2372* | **Unedited on purpose**: `stage-config`'s `:lower` delegates to `lower-packet`, so `lower-transform` / `open-stage` / `step-stage` (`:2375-2403`) inherit finalization. This is the design's \"streaming stage\" leg. |\n   138\t| `src/cljc/yang/typescript/antlr/prelude.cljc` | **4364-4370** | The linked **`js`** module tree `module-uast` → `(u/annotate-call-sites (core/module-tree module-definitions []))`; docstring extended with the \"markers publish beside its manifest, the manifest keeps schema 1 and its address does not move\" rationale. Byte-for-byte the shape already landed in the read-only core at `yang/core/call.cljc:168-175` and in `yang/clojure/prelude.cljc:108-112`. No `:require` line changed (`yang.core.uast :as u` was already there at `:68`). |\n   139\t| `src/cljc/yang/typescript/antlr/safepoint.cljc` | **186-197** | The linked **`jssp`** module tree `module-uast` → annotated the same way. In scope per design `:278` (\"Cover … bundled and linked `js`, `yang.call`, **and safepoint runtime**\") and `:161` (family 1 names \"TypeScript **`js/jssp`**\"). See judgement call J1. |\n   140\t\n   141\t### 1.2 Existing-test repairs — the complete blast radius was 6 assertions in 3 files\n   142\t\n   143\t| File | Lines | Repair |\n   144\t|---|---|---|\n   145\t| `test/yang/typescript/antlr/lower_test.clj` | **71-79** | The golden builder `cells` (used only by `var-declaration-golden-test`) wraps its result in `u/annotate-call-sites`. Repairs the three goldens at `:90` (`\"var x = 1;\"`), `:96` (`\"let y = 2;\"`), `:102` (`\"let z;\"`). |\n   146\t| | **140-145** | `literal-golden-test`'s BigInt expectation — the `js/string->bigint` application — wrapped in `u/annotate-call-sites`. |\n   147\t| `test/yang/typescript/antlr/lower_portable_test.cljc` | **206-217** | `hand-packet-golden-test`'s literal expected tree wrapped in `u/annotate-call-sites`. **This was the only portable breaking site**, i.e. it would have gone red on Node and Dart as well as the JVM. |\n   148\t| `test/yang/typescript/antlr/linked_prelude_test.cljc` | **61-63** | `jssp-module-uast-is-one-wide-application-test`: `(dissoc (last operands) :tail?)` → `(dissoc (last operands) :tail? :yang/call-site)`, extending the file's own existing `:tail?`-stripping idiom rather than inventing a new one. Broken only because I marked `jssp` (J1). The sibling assertion at `:67-70` targets a `:literal` and needed no change. |\n   149\t\n   150\t**Repair idiom chosen:** finalize the *expected* side with the same generic walker,\n   151\trather than stripping the *actual* side. A stripped comparison stops pinning the\n   152\tmarking; `(u/annotate-call-sites <literal tree>)` keeps each golden a literal,\n   153\thand-written tree and additionally pins that the producer's output is *exactly* the\n   154\tshared walk's output over it. The repo's only prior art for the stripping direction is\n   155\tthe private `strip-call-sites` at `test/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc:645-651`, used\n   360\t\n   361\t### 4.3 Address / hash invariance — the chain verified by reading\n   362\t\n   363\t`vm/ast->semantic-bytecode` hashes only §2.3 grammar slots and drops other node keys\n   364\t(`yin/vm.cljc:1113-1186`), so `:root` and `:rows` are byte-identical marked or not.\n   365\tDownstream: `publish.cljc:353-358` materializes the **schema-1** manifest first and the C1\n   366\tside table never enters it (*\"so identical specifications under distinct admissions share\n   367\tone manifest address\"*); `derive/stack-image` returns `{:image … :side-table …}` and\n   368\t`cond->`s `:call-provenance` **beside** `:image`\n   369\t(`yin/vm/semantic/derive.cljc:152-159`); `derive/register-image` assoc's it onto an\n   370\totherwise identical image (`:229-239`) and `publish.cljc:340-347` hashes `(:image …)` /\n   371\t`(dissoc register-full :call-provenance)`. So flipping `js` and `jssp` from the unclaimed\n   372\tlane to the claimed lane changes the *side* artifacts (a `:call-sites` key on the\n   373\tpublication result, a manifest record, provenance segments) and **not** the tree address,\n   374\tthe semantic/stack/register image hashes, `h-address`/`r-address`, or the manifest address.\n   375\tIndependent corroboration that the claimed lane is already production-proven for a ts\n   376\tcomposition: `yang.core.call/module-uast` has been C1-marked since cc1\n   377\t(`yang/core/call.cljc:168-175`) and `linked_harness`'s `published` delay publishes it\n   378\t*first*, into the same store. This is the mechanism satisfying brief requirement 2, and\n   379\t`canonical-invariance-test` pins it.\n   380\t\n   381\tAlso verified unaffected: `core/free-name-vec` over the newly-marked `module-uast`\n   382\t(`yang/core/prelude.cljc:80-96` branches on `(:type node)` and returns `acc` for any\n   383\tnon-map value, so the marker's value `1` is a no-op and the key is never visited);\n   384\t`core/module-spec` (`:138-159`) is AST-shape-agnostic; `vm/ast->datoms` writes only\n   385\tgrammar fields.\n   386\t\n   387\t### 4.4 One real observable delta, decided consciously\n   388\t\n   389\t`safepoint/derive-envelope` on a ts envelope changes behaviour. Today `derive-call-sites`\n   390\t(`yang/safepoint.cljc:298-386`) finds no C1 rows and answers nil, so the derived envelope\n   391\tcarries `:yin/frontend-metadata []` and **no** `:yang.safepoint/correspondence`. After this\n   392\tchange it answers rows plus a correspondence. **No ts caller supplies `:injected-origin`** —\n   393\t`safepoint/transform` (`:455`) calls the 3-arity, as do\n   394\t`test/yang/typescript/antlr/e2e_test.clj:71-86`, `safepoint_test.clj:132-136`, and\n   395\t`linked_prelude_test.cljc:249-262` — so the injected hook applications stay **unclaimed by\n   396\tdesign** (`safepoint.cljc:303-306`: *\"without one it is recorded as injected and left\n   397\tunclaimed\"*) and the derived envelope's C1 rows deliberately do **not** cover the derived\n   398\ttree. That is safe today only because nothing re-projects a derived envelope: all four ts\n   399\tcall sites stop at `vm/semantic-bytecode->ast` / `tree-of` / `vm/validate-rows`, and\n   400\t`check-projected-claim!` fires only on `project-member`'s already-projected arm\n   401\t(`encoder.cljc:112-121`). **If any future ts host routes a derived envelope back through\n   402\t`encoder/project` or `encoder/load`, it will refuse\n   403\t`:yang/call-site-incomplete-coverage` until it supplies `:injected-origin`.** A latent trap,\n   404\tnot a present defect. See judgement call **J3**.\n   405\t\n   406\tNo ts test asserts either way, and `insertion-is-deterministic-test` stays green because\n   407\t`derive-call-sites` is deterministic (sorts by `jing/canonical-compare` and\n   408\t`(sort-by (comp pr-str key) by-path)`).\n   414\tand `src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/` — the only `call-site` hits in the python prelude are prose\n   415\tabout `*args`/`**kwargs` (`prelude.cljc:1110`, `:1113`). So the two sibling adoption rounds\n   416\tare still ahead, and `source_call_test.cljc`'s unguarded donor helper (§4.2) is theirs to fix.\n   417\t\n   418\t---\n   419\t\n   420\t## 5. The equality gate — what I could and could not gather locally\n   421\t\n   422\tThe adopted ruling (`collab/yang-call/1794980000000-orchestrator-two-relays-equality-and-h36-audit-inputs.md:10`,\n   423\tadopted verbatim at `collab/yang-call/1795010000000-orchestrator-reply-equality-gate-per-frontend.md:6,9`):\n   424\t*\"the cross-host occurrence-key equality gate is part of EACH frontend's own acceptance —\n   425\tnot a separate post-all-three gate … it never compares across frontends … the per-frontend\n   426\tgates are the whole gate.\"* Design `:266-272` defines what must be equal: identical final\n   427\tcanonical roots and the full set of `[origin root path]` keys on JVM, Node and Dart (plus\n   428\tJolt for the mandatory portable paths); identical C1 rows and per-format instruction\n   429\tprovenance; for TS/PHP packet routes, *\"compare compilation of the same source-derived\n   430\tvalidated CST\"*; and a separate negative fixture where identical text under two distinct\n   431\tsupplied admission tokens must demand different origins.\n   432\t\n   433\t**Evidence gathered by execution: NONE.** No lane was run — not JVM, not Node, not Dart, not\n   434\tJolt. I have zero `Ran N tests` lines to report.\n   435\t\n   436\tWhat was built instead, and what it is worth:\n   437\t\n   438\t1. **The fixture is host-independent by construction.** Every packet is hand-built through\n   439\t   `lower-portable-test`'s public builders, whose ids are preorder *\"as the parser numbers\n   440\t   them\"*. No local parser runs, which is exactly design `:271`'s TS leg — *\"This proves\n   441\t   compilation equality, not nonexistent local-parser parity.\"* The file is `.cljc` and uses\n   442\t   the reference's `#?(:cljd Object :clj Exception :cljs :default)` catch idiom, so it loads\n   443\t   on all three lanes. The ts local-parser restriction (`docs/design/yang.typescript.md:113-116,517-518`)\n   444\t   is therefore never touched.\n   445\t2. **`cross-host-equality-test`** is the local half of the gate, in three legs: (a) two\n   446\t   independent lowerings of one packet answer one root and one coordinate set, and that set\n   447\t   equals the occurrence relation recomputed from canonical rows alone; (b) an\n   448\t   **independently finalized literal tree** — the `var x = 1;` module body re-expressed by\n   449\t   hand as `u/app`/`u/lam`/`u/then`/`u/lit` source inside the test — answers the *same* root\n   450\t   address and the *same* `[root path]` set as `lower-module-body` of the packet, so the\n   451\t   paths are pinned as literal source data and a lane whose path arithmetic differed would\n   452\t   fail against a literal, not against another host's answer; (c) the root node's *kind*\n   453\t   decides whether `[]` is a coordinate (`lower-module-body` → `:application` root → `[]`\n   454\t   claimed; `lower-unit` → `:lambda` root → `[]` not claimed), and every composed production\n   455\t   tree claims its own root.\n   456\t3. **`equality-gate-test`** runs the reference's core assertion over all eleven production\n   457\t   trees: the eligible set — derived in-test from `vm/application-occurrences` and the row\n   458\t   tags, independently of the producer's walk — EQUALS the marker set, on both the\n   459\t   origin-bearing and the origin-free `[root path]` projection; both validators answer true;\n   460\t   and every row is exactly the core's 5-coordinate tuple under one root.\n   461\t4. **`stage-envelope-test`** pins origin semantics on the real streaming-stage envelope for\n   462\t   both profiles: coordinates carry the **stage's** admission origin\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_20","type":"agent_message","text":"The four lowering seams and both published module trees use the shared finalizer after assembly. Their coverage tests would catch a missing finalizer. The coordinate test has a narrower blind spot: it computes both sides through the same path machinery, so it lacks the reference suite’s literal path pin.\n\nSafepoint undercoverage matches the shared API’s documented behavior when no injected origin is supplied. It needs a named completion obligation and a TS regression test; it cannot count as complete C1 adoption for derived programs. I’m also distinguishing the golden repairs: five finalize expected values, while the sixth strips the new marker from the produced `require` node.\n"}}
