alidation-failure-test` `:364` | `validation-failure-test` | all nine rules: identical-delivery dedupe; `-conflict`; `-unsupported-version`; `-nonexistent-path`; `-non-application`; `-incomplete-coverage`; `-malformed` (4- and 6-coordinate rows); `-duplicate-entry` under `{:declared? true}`; `-multi-claim` in all three validator modes plus the `:site`/`:origins` diagnostic contents. The non-application target path is **derived** from `vm/occurrences` + row tags (sorted by `pr-str` for host independence) rather than hardcoded, so it cannot rot |\n   503\t| 5 | `safepoint-independence-test` `:466` | `safepoint-independence-test` | the `:loop` and `[:call \"f\" 0]` marks still reach `safepoint/sites`; the two keys never cross rows; the relation's keyword keys are exactly `#{:yang/call-site :yang/site}` (**no ts-private table**); coverage validates over the combined relation; and the mechanism split pinned both directions — the safepoint mark exists only in node `meta` and never as a plain key, the C1 marker only as a plain key and never in `meta` |\n   504\t| 6 | `canonical-invariance-test` `:512` | `canonical-invariance-test` | identical `:root` **and** `:rows` marked vs stripped over all 11 trees; identical `sr-linearize/project` `:vector` and `:address`; the key present in `:yin/frontend-metadata` while absent from `pr-str` of `:yin/batch` and `:yin/source-positions` — brief requirement 2 (unitarity) pinned directly |\n   505\t| 7 | `encoder-claim-test` `:549` | `encoder-claim-test` | `program-batch` on a finalized ts tree answers a **6**-element batch with verdict `[true]` (this member now *claims*); dropping one marker refuses with `-incomplete-coverage`; a version-2 marker refuses with `-unsupported-version`; a fully stripped tree still yields the **5**-element unclaimed shape — the additive-compatibility pin (design `:157`) |\n   506\t| 8 | `publication-claim-test` `:583` (helper `:569`) | `published-module-test` | for `js` and `jssp`: the root is a marked wide 