{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_29","type":"agent_message","text":"Completed-GMT: 2026-11-12 23:13:44 GMT\nCompleted-Local: 2026-11-13 06:13:44 Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh\n\n**Verdict: FIX-LIST.** The TS finalization placement is sound. Two test pins need strengthening, and the J3 safety argument overlooks an inherited metadata-loss path in the shared encoder.\n\nReviewed `b134207f..603d2d4e`, including both commits. No files edited; no JVM suites rerun. Reported execution results remain orchestrator evidence.\n\n| Severity | File:line | Invariant / evidence | Recommended correction |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **P1 — inherited core boundary gap** | [encoder.cljc:158](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-callsite/src/cljc/yin/vm/encoder.cljc:158) | Re-projecting a safepoint-derived envelope **silently drops its C1 rows**, contrary to the engineer’s claimed incomplete-coverage refusal. [Safepoint:441](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-callsite/src/cljc/yang/safepoint.cljc:441) puts rows on the envelope; encoder reads only each member’s `:frontend-metadata` at line 115, then replaces the envelope table at line 158. Derived members contain canonical rows without that member-local table. | Correct the findings and add a TS derivative regression. Assign the shared encoder owner to preserve and validate envelope-level tables, or explicitly refuse this input. Keep derived-envelope re-projection outside accepted C1 routes until resolved. This defect is outside the reviewed diff. |\n| **P2 — coordinate pin is not independent** | [typescript_callsite_test.cljc:642](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-callsite/test/yang/typescript_callsite_test.cljc:642) | The “literal” golden pins AST structure, but both coordinate sets still pass through the same projection machinery. No nonempty structural path is asserted literally. A consistent path-numbering error in extraction and enumeration can pass locally. The reference suite explicitly pins paths at `clojure_callsite_test.cljc:119`. | Add literal expected paths and a reviewed root pin for a small fixture. Add the design’s distinct-admission-token negative fixture. Compare full `[origin root path]` sets in the downstream host gate. |\n| **P2 — closed-set audit omits hook definitions** | [typescript_callsite_test.cljc:714](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-callsite/test/yang/typescript_callsite_test.cljc:714) | Both closed-set scans inspect only `prelude/definitions`. `hooks/function-definitions` receives export-name checks and live export/definition equality only. A neutrally named `js.sp` wrapper calling `cell/dsg__provenance` would pass this audit. | Apply the empty private-door-user and guest-C1-key assertions to hook definitions too. Include a renamed hook-wrapper negative fixture. |\n\n**1. Self-judged stage repair: ACCEPT.**\n\nThe [design of record](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/yang-clojure/1794670000000-architect-callsite-generalization-design.gpt-6-astra.findings.md:65) requires finalization at executable ingress (§2.3, line 65), explicitly includes TS stage production (lines 133 and 278), and assigns origin ownership to the admitting composition (lines 38–39).\n\nAccordingly, bundled runtime applications must receive markers under the stage admission origin. Zero markers overall would be wrong. The repaired helper actually filters by origin at [test:154](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-callsite/test/yang/typescript_callsite_test.cljc:154); lines 313–319 assert coverage under the admission origin, absence under the unrelated fixture origin, and exactly one marker origin. This is a justified correction.\n\nThe citation to design line 139 needs qualification: it describes the existing packet-unit token **and requires an audit of fresh admissions versus retries**. The single-admission test does not discharge that freshness requirement.\n\n**2. Four judgement calls:**\n\n| Call | Ruling | Contract judgment |\n|---|---|---|\n| **(a) Mark `jssp` publication trees** | **ACCEPT** | Design lines 161 and 278 explicitly include `js/jssp` and the safepoint runtime. Finalizing `module-uast` at [safepoint.cljc:195](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-callsite/src/cljc/yang/typescript/antlr/safepoint.cljc:195) is correct. |\n| **(b) Leave bundled fragments unmarked until owning finalization** | **ACCEPT** | Design lines 65 and 138 permit fragment deferral. `lower-packet` and `lower-units` finalize after runtime composition and tail marking. This permission does not establish complete C1 coverage for separately assembled safepointed programs. |\n| **(c) Omit `:injected-origin`** | **NAMED OBLIGATION — TS-SP-C1** | The shared API explicitly supports surviving rows plus unclaimed injected occurrences. That is a partial correspondence result, not complete derived-tree adoption. The admitting composition must supply genuine helper-admission provenance before claiming complete coverage. Existing TS consumers reconstruct executable ASTs without re-projecting the derived envelope; their execution success does not establish C1 completeness. Resolve the encoder finding above before accepting that route. |\n| **(d) Borrow the validator from `yang.clojure`** | **ACCEPT** | This is test-only reuse of the existing portable validator, consistent with `core/uast.cljc:125`. No parallel validator was introduced. Record a shared-owner cleanup to move the language-neutral contract into `yang.core`; it is not required for this TS patch. |\n\n**3. Blind-authored test strength: mixed.**\n\nThe coverage equality test is substantive. [Production inventory:239](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-callsite/test/yang/typescript_callsite_test.cljc:239) directly exercises all four lowering seams, both publication trees, and bundled/linked compositions. The nonempty-marker assertion, exact eligible/marked equality, and strict AST validation at lines 278–285 would catch a missing finalizer at any of those seams.\n\nA coordinate error affecting only emitted markers would also fail. A consistent error shared by extraction and enumeration lacks an independent literal-path check: **P2 above**.\n\nThe export audit **does catch a renamed `js` wrapper** retaining a reserved-door reference: its body scan would make `door-users` nonempty. Its corresponding `jssp` protection is missing: **P2 above**. Freezing every export name is unnecessary to fix that specific gap.\n\n**4. Golden repairs: original semantic precision preserved, with one reporting correction.**\n\nFive assertions finalize the expected side:\n\n- Three declaration goldens through [lower_test.clj:76](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-callsite/test/yang/typescript/antlr/lower_test.clj:76).\n- The BigInt application at line 140.\n- The portable whole-tree golden at [lower_portable_test.cljc:207](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-callsite/test/yang/typescript/antlr/lower_portable_test.cljc:207).\n\nThe sixth instead strips the new marker from the produced `require` node at [linked_prelude_test.cljc:62](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-callsite/test/yang/typescript/antlr/linked_prelude_test.cljc:62). Thus “all six finalized EXPECTED” is inaccurate. That comparison retains its original exact structural precision, and the new module coverage test independently checks the marker. No precise comparison became a superset match.\n\n**5. Scope and invariant sweep: passed for the changed production code.**\n\nThe diff contains exactly seven files; no generic core, VM, encoder, linker, or Clojure frontend edits appear. The four lowering seams and two publication trees use the existing shared finalizer. No new `dsg__` calls or doors were introduced.\n\nMarkers remain outside grammar-hashed content and manifests. The finalizer preserves other keys and node metadata; the canonical-invariance tests compare roots and rows across the production inventory. No new mutable state, callback mechanism, or interpretation/execution coupling appears.\n\nThe encoder finding is an inherited preservation gap exposed by this review, not a defect in TS finalizer placement. Resolve the fix-list and record TS-SP-C1 and admission-freshness obligations explicitly. Node/Dart/Jolt checks, full cross-host equality, and the remaining acceptance evidence stay with the downstream owners; this review does not waive them."}}
